  planner_response {
    response: "Here is the exact blueprint for **how** to implement this benchmark and multi-backend execution strategy step-by-step:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Export & Pull the Current Environment Snapshot\nTo get everything out of the Google sandbox and into your local / repo workspace:\n1. **Export the Codebase**: In the top-right settings/export menu of Google AI Studio, click **Export to GitHub** (or **Download ZIP**).\n2. **Inspect the Artifacts**: Unpack the files (`package.json`, `/components`, `/services`, `/hooks`, etc.).\n3. **Run Locally or in Cloudflare Containers**:\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   npm run build\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Define the `ExecutionEnvironment` Abstraction\nIn your AgentSam architecture, wrap execution targets behind a unified TypeScript/Python interface so the agent harness doesn\'t care if it\'s running inside a Cloudflare Container, a local PTY, or a Google Antigravity session.\n\n```typescript\nexport interface ToolExecutionResult {\n  stdout: string;\n  stderr: string;\n  exitCode: number;\n  durationMs: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ExecutionEnvironment {\n  id: string;\n  type: \'local\' | \'cloudflare_container\' | \'gcp_vm\' | \'google_antigravity\';\n  \n  // Core primitives\n  execCommand(cmd: string, cwd?: string): Promise<ToolExecutionResult>;\n  readFile(path: string): Promise<string>;\n  writeFile(path: string, content: string): Promise<void>;\n  listFiles(dir: string): Promise<string[]>;\n  \n  // Telemetry & metrics\n  getMetrics(): {\n    totalDurationMs: number;\n    toolCallCount: number;\n    tokensConsumed: { input: number; output: number; thinking: number };\n    estimatedCostUsd: number;\n  };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Run the Side-by-Side Autonomous Mission Benchmark\n\nExecute the exact same mission on both backends and capture telemetry:\n\n#### The Mission Prompt:\n```text\nMISSION: Audit repository for competing identity authorities.\n- Do not modify files.\n- Use shell/grep/file tools autonomously.\n- Identify duplicate auth/session/token logic with file paths and line references.\n- Generate an architecture map (SVG).\n- Produce a consolidation sequence report.\n- Stop when the report is rendered.\n```\n\n#### Metrics to Log & Compare:\n| Metric | AgentSam + Cloudflare Sandbox | Google Antigravity |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Duration (Wall-clock)** | *e.g., 4m 12s* | *e.g., 2m 45s* |\n| **Tool Calls Executed** | Count (grep, cat, ls, node) | Count (view, run_command, edit) |\n| **Input / Output Tokens** | Tracked via Model Gateway | Tracked via Gemini Token Stream |\n| **Thinking Tokens** | e.g., 3.7 Flash Thinking | Included in session stream |\n| **Compute Cost** | Cloudflare Container compute (~$0.0007) | $0.00 (Preview) |\n| **Model Cost** | Calculated per million tokens | Calculated per million tokens |\n| **Effective Total Cost** | **$X.XX** | **$Y.YY** |\n| **Interventions Required** | 0 (or count of halts) | 0 (or count of halts) |\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: What about `files.pythonhosted.org` & Network Policies?\nIn your observation:\n- `files.pythonhosted.org` is the official PyPI content delivery network (used when `pip install` or Python packages are fetched).\n- **Google Antigravity\'s Network Allowlist**: Managed sandboxes use an egress firewall allowing standard package registries (PyPI, npm, GitHub, Google APIs) while blocking arbitrary unvetted endpoints to prevent data exfiltration.\n- **In Cloudflare Containers**: You can mirror this policy by routing egress through Cloudflare Gateway / DNS filtering or confining network access at the Worker/DO layer.\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: The Strategic Path Forward\n1. **Use Antigravity as a benchmark engine** while sandbox compute is $0.\n2. **Keep Cloudflare as your sovereign execution layer** so you own data boundaries and pricing predictability.\n3. **Capture the telemetry**: If Gemini 3.7 Flash + Antigravity completes a 30-tool mission for $0.20\342\200\223$0.40 total, that sets the baseline efficiency target for your custom AgentSam loop."
