s autonomously.\n- Identify duplicate auth/session/token logic with file paths and line references.\n- Generate an architecture map (SVG).\n- Produce a consolidation sequence report.\n- Stop when the report is rendered.\n```\n\n#### Metrics to Log & Compare:\n| Metric | AgentSam + Cloudflare Sandbox | Google Antigravity |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Duration (Wall-clock)** | *e.g., 4m 12s* | *e.g., 2m 45s* |\n| **Tool Calls Executed** | Count (grep, cat, ls, node) | Count (view, run_command, edit) |\n| **Input / Output Tokens** | Tracked via Model Gateway | Tracked via Gemini Token Stream |\n| **Thinking Tokens** | e.g., 3.7 Flash Thinking | Included in session stream |\n| **Compute Cost** | Cloudflare Container compute (~$0.0007) | $0.00 (Preview) |\n| **Model Cost** | Calculated per million tokens | Calculated per million tokens |\n| **Effective Total Cost** | **$X.XX** | **$Y.YY** |\n| **Interventions Required** | 0 (or count of halts) | 0 (or count of halts) |\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: What about `files.pythonhosted.org` & Network Policies?\nIn your observation:\n- `files.pythonhosted.org` is the official PyPI content delivery network (used when `pip install` or Python packages are fetched).\n- **Google Antigravity\'s Network Allowlist**: Managed sandboxes use an egress firewall allowing standard package registries (PyPI, npm, GitHub, Google APIs) while blocking arbitrary unvetted endpoints to prevent data exfiltration.\n- **In Cloudflare Containers**: You can mirror this policy by routing egress through Cloudflare Gateway / DNS filtering or confining network access at the Worker/DO layer.\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: The Strategic Path Forward\n1. **Use Antigravity as a benchmark engine** while sandbox compute is $0.\n2. **Keep Cloudflare as your sovereign execution layer** so you own data boundaries and pricing predictability.\n3. **Capture the telemetry**: If Gemini 3.7 Flash + Antigravity completes a 30-tool mission for $0.20\342\200\223$0.40 total, that sets the base