    response: "I have updated the application with an app shell, live theme engine, and settings interface:\n\n- **Application Shell & Window Chrome**: Added an application frame featuring desktop-style window controls (close, minimize, maximize toggle), an active Gemini Engine status badge with a glowing pulse indicator, a quick 1-click theme cycler with color swatches, and a dedicated **Settings & Theme Engine** trigger (`Ctrl/Cmd + ,`).\n- **Live Theme Studio (`AppSettingsModal`)**: Built a settings dialog with live preview and local storage persistence:\n  - **8 Presets**: *Obsidian Stealth (Default Dark)*, *Deep Void (Pure AMOLED)*, *Midnight Sapphire (Deep Blue)*, *Cyberpunk Neon (Violet & Pink)*, *Emerald Matrix (Phosphor Green)*, *Solar Amber (Warm Charcoal & Gold)*, *Google Clean (Crisp Light)*, and *Nordic Ice (Frost Light)*.\n  - **Live Customization**: Custom accent color picker, UI density toggles (Compact, Default, Spacious), corner radius controls (Sharp, Modern, Rounded), typography selection, canvas backdrop pattern switcher (Dots, Grid, Vignette, Clean), and speech synthesis defaults.\n- **CSS Variable Mapping**: Mapped all browser surfaces, tabs, navigation buttons, omnibar states, and modals to responsive CSS custom properties (`--app-bg`, `--app-surface-1`, `--app-accent`, `--app-border`, `--app-radius-base`, etc.) for seamless real-time recoloring without flicker or reload."
    modified_response: "I have updated the application with an app shell, live theme engine, and settings interface:\n\n- **Application Shell & Window Chrome**: Added an application frame featuring desktop-style window controls (close, minimize, maximize toggle), an active Gemini Engine status badge with a glowing pulse indicator, a quick 1-click theme cycler with color swatches, and a dedicated **Settings & Theme Engine** trigger (`Ctrl/Cmd + ,`).\n- **Live Theme Studio (`AppSettingsModal`)**: Built a settings dialog with live preview and local storage persistence:\n  - **8 Presets**: *Obsidian Stealth (Default Dark)*, *Deep Void (Pure AMOLED)*, *Midnight Sapphire (Deep Blue)*, *Cyberpunk Neon (Violet & Pink)*, *Emerald Matrix (Phosphor Green)*, *Solar Amber (Warm Charcoal & Gold)*, *Google Clean (Crisp Light)*, and *Nordic Ice (Frost Light)*.\n  - **Live Customization**: Custom accent color picker, UI density toggles (Compact, Default, Spacious), corner radius controls (Sharp, Modern, Rounded), typography selection, canvas backdrop pattern switcher (Dots, Grid, Vignette, Clean), and speech synthesis defaults.\n- **CSS Variable Mapping**: Mapped all browser surfaces, tabs, navigation buttons, omnibar states, and modals to responsive CSS custom properties (`--app-bg`, `--app-surface-1`, `--app-accent`, `--app-border`, `--app-radius-base`, etc.) for seamless real-time recoloring without flicker or reload."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787970896
      nanos: 170227573
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "add Yeah \342\200\224 I checked Cloudflare\342\200\231s current stack as of today, plus the shape of your current main, and there\342\200\231s a much shorter path than continuing to hand-build every piece of a Cursor replacement.\n\nThe biggest discovery is that Cloudflare has basically converged on the architecture we\342\200\231ve been circling around.\n\nThe new centerpiece: @cloudflare/computer\n\nCloudflare released @cloudflare/computer on August 3 specifically for agents that need to work on real codebases. Their own framing is essentially: an agent needs a computer, not a container.\n\nIt gives an agent:\n\npersistent SQLite-backed filesystem\nread\nwrite\nedit\nls\nexec\nGit/repository operations\nauditing/gating\nmultiple execution backends\n\nAnd the clever part is that not every command spins up Linux.\n\nAgent Sam\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\226\274\nWorkspace / Computer\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Worker isolate\n   \342\224\202     grep\n   \342\224\202     cat\n   \342\224\202     sed\n   \342\224\202     jq\n   \342\224\202     file edits\n   \342\224\202     searches\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Linux container\n         npm install\n         npm test\n         vite build\n         git\n         native binaries\n         long-running server\n\nThe Worker backend uses just-bash + Dynamic Workers for cheap textual work; the container is lazily reached only when a real Linux userland is necessary. One workspace can have both backends simultaneously.\n\nThat is almost exactly the execution router we\'ve been trying to evolve AgentSam toward.\n\nOne caveat: @cloudflare/computer is explicitly preview-only and not recommended as a production dependency yet. So I would put it behind AgentSam\'s execution contract, not make the whole product depend directly on it.\n\nThen Cloudflare quietly solved another huge AgentSam problem: Code Mode\n\nThis one may be even more important for the Cursor replacement.\n\nRight now a traditional agent often does:\n\nmodel\n \342\206\223\nfs_search\n \342\206\223\nmodel\n \342\206\223\nfs_read\n \342\206\223\nmodel\n \342\206\223\nfs_read\n \342\206\223\nmodel\n \342\206\223\ngrep\n \342\206\223\nmodel\n \342\206\223\ngit_diff\n \342\206\223\nmodel\n\nEvery damn little operation creates another model round trip.\n\nCloudflare Code Mode lets the model instead write a small program that composes tools:\n\nconst files = await tools.search(\"resolveIdentity\");\n\nconst relevant = files\n  .filter(...)\n  .slice(0, 20);\n\nconst contents = await Promise.all(\n  relevant.map(f => tools.read(f.path))\n);\n\nreturn analyze(contents);\n\nOne model decision can therefore perform a whole mini-workflow of dependent operations, loops, filtering, branching, and result shaping. Cloudflare specifically recommends it for large tool catalogs and multi-step work.\n\nThat attacks two of AgentSam\'s current problems simultaneously:\n\ntool-call count explosion and huge MCP schema/context overhead.\n\nIt can also expose your existing MCP tools through Code Mode instead of dumping every MCP schema into every turn. Cloudflare added durable MCP Code Mode integration, discovery, approvals and execution history.\n\nThat is the thing I would prioritize.\n\nAnd the model situation just got ridiculous\n\nThis happened basically yesterday.\n\nCloudflare added GLM-5.3, explicitly positioning it as a long-running agentic coding model. It gets a 1,048,576-token context window, function calling, reasoning and structured outputs. Cloudflare cites dramatic improvements over GLM-5.2 on terminal and long-horizon software-engineering benchmarks.\n\nPricing:\n\nGLM-5.3\n\n$1.40 / M input\n$0.26 / M cached input\n$4.40 / M output\n\nBut the one I\'d hit constantly is the new GLM-5.3 Flash.\n\nCloudflare says it outperforms GLM-5.2 across its comparisons while approaching Claude Opus 4.8 on coding/agentic benchmarks, and it has the same 1M context plus vision/function-calling/reasoning.\n\nIts price is:\n\nGLM-5.3 Flash\n\n$0.15 / M input\n$0.03 / M cached input\n$0.50 / M output\n\nThat is the model I would make the AgentSam workhorse.\n\nNot the expensive model.\n\nAgentSam\'s model ladder becomes stupidly simple\n                   AgentSam Mission\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                    AI Gateway\n                         \342\224\202\n             \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n             \342\224\202                      \342\224\202\n             \342\226\274                      \342\226\274\n       GLM-5.3 Flash            GLM-5.3\n        DEFAULT                  ESCALATE\n      $0.15 / M in             $1.40 / M in\n      $0.50 / M out            $4.40 / M out\n             \342\224\202\n             \342\224\202 failure / high complexity\n             \342\226\274\n       provider fallback\n   Gemini / OpenAI / Anthropic\n\nCloudflare AI Gateway can now implement that routing without us hard-coding it into AgentSam.\n\nDynamic Routing supports conditions, model fallbacks, quotas, rate limits, budget limits and versioned routes.\n\nAnd this is especially relevant after burning the Cursor budget:\n\nCloudflare added actual dollar spend limits.\n\nYou can say effectively:\n\nAgentSam\ndaily budget: $5\n\nGLM Flash:\n    normal use\n\nGLM 5.3:\n    maximum $2/day\n\nexpensive external providers:\n    maximum $1/day\n\nbudget exhausted:\n    fall back to cheaper model\n\nAI Gateway will calculate model costs and enforce it, including BYOK requests.\n\nThat should become non-negotiable for AgentSam.\n\nNo more discovering the bill after the agent went wild.\n\nCloudflare also basically built our Browser lane\n\nYou already peeled MYBROWSER into its own backend domain.\n\nGood decision.\n\nCloudflare renamed Browser Rendering \342\206\222 Browser Run, and agents can now control real Chrome through CDP by writing code rather than being limited to a dozen browser_click, browser_navigate, etc. actions.\n\nBut the newest interesting part is Kitesurf.\n\nIt\'s an agent-first browser running in Workers rather than Chromium. Cloudflare says common agent workloads use 3\342\200\2237\303\227 less CPU/memory, and it\'s currently free during beta.\n\nSo MYBROWSER could eventually route:\n\nNeed webpage understanding?\n        \342\224\202\n        \342\226\274\n    Kitesurf\n    cheap / fast\n        \342\224\202\n        \342\224\202 insufficient?\n        \342\226\274\n     Chromium\n    full browser\n\nPerfect for:\n\nchange frontend\n      \342\206\223\ndeploy preview\n      \342\206\223\nopen page\n      \342\206\223\naccessibility tree\n      \342\206\223\ninspect console\n      \342\206\223\nscreenshot\n      \342\206\223\ncompare\n      \342\206\223\nrepair\n\nAnd Browser Run now has structured human handoff and an accessibility-tree endpoint specifically useful to agents.\n\nThat gets us much closer to:\n\n\342\200\234Fix the mobile composer.\342\200\235\n\ninstead of:\n\n\342\200\234write some CSS and tell Sam to see whether it worked.\342\200\235\n\nThe actual AgentSam I\'d build now\n\nNot another architecture rewrite.\n\nThis:\n\n                    AGENTSAM\n                       \342\224\202\n                       \342\226\274\n              @cloudflare/think\n         session / streaming / memory\n                       \342\224\202\n                       \342\226\274\n                 runTurn()\n                       \342\224\202\n             \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n             \342\224\202                   \342\224\202\n        direct tools         Code Mode\n        simple action       multi-tool plan\n             \342\224\202                   \342\224\202\n             \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                       \342\226\274\n             AgentSam Workspace\n                       \342\224\202\n        \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\274\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n        \342\224\202              \342\224\202               \342\224\202\n        \342\226\274              \342\226\274               \342\226\274\n    Computer       Sandbox          Local Mac\n    Worker         Container        localpty\n    isolate          Linux\n        \342\224\202              \342\224\202\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                \342\224\202\n                \342\226\274\n            repository\n                \342\224\202\n        \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n        \342\226\274                \342\226\274\n     Git/GitHub       Browser Run\n                         \342\224\202\n                   Kitesurf / Chrome\n\n@cloudflare/think is now a pretty serious harness itself: durable-object state, persisted messages, streaming, resumability, agentic tool loops, client tools and sub-agents.\n\nCloudflare also added detached background sub-agents with durable progress and milestones, which survive disconnects/evictions.\n\nSo a build mission could become:\n\nMISSION\nRepair mobile chat composer\n       \342\224\202\n       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Inspector\n       \342\224\202     repo search\n       \342\224\202\n       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Builder\n       \342\224\202     edits + tests\n       \342\224\202\n       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Browser verifier\n             live page + screenshot\n\nwhile the parent AgentSam remains responsive.\n\nDon\'t put Workflows everywhere\n\nThis is important given all the overlap we\'ve been ripping out.\n\nUse:\n\nAgent/DO\nfor interactive mission state.\n\nCode Mode\nfor a burst of related tool operations.\n\nComputer/Sandbox\nfor execution.\n\nDetached sub-agent\nfor another intelligent worker.\n\nWorkflow\nonly when execution genuinely needs durable sleeps/retries/checkpoints across long periods.\n\nCloudflare themselves describe Agents as real-time state/communication and Workflows as durable execution.\n\nSo don\'t create:\n\nAgent\n \342\206\222 Workflow\n   \342\206\222 Queue\n     \342\206\222 Agent\n       \342\206\222 Workflow\n         \342\206\222 Container\n\nfor every shell command.\n\nThat\'s exactly the infrastructure lasagna you\'ve been trying to delete.\n\nI checked current main, too\n\nYou\'re much closer than starting over.\n\nThe current tree already has:\n\napp/agentsam/frontend/workbench/browser/\nbackend/\ncontainers/\nagentsam-sdk/\n\nand a substantial browser workbench already exists.\n\nInterestingly, when I searched main for the actual new Cloudflare runtime imports, I found the Agents/Sandbox material primarily in your .cursor/rules/cloudflare-*.mdc documentation rather than the application runtime itself.\n\nSo we haven\'t missed some giant finished integration.\n\nThere is a clean opportunity to introduce this behind the backend AgentSam boundary without ripping up the frontend again.\n\nI would not port that Antigravity Python demo wholesale.\n\nThe first vertical slice\n\nI would make exactly one thing work:\n\nAgentSam receives an InnerAnimalMedia engineering mission and finishes it.\n\nSomething like:\n\nFix the mobile chat composer.\nInspect existing implementation first.\nDo not create duplicate ownership.\nRun relevant tests.\nOpen the production/preview UI.\nVerify the repair visually.\nCommit only after verification.\n\nAnd AgentSam should visibly do:\n\n\342\227\217 Preparing workspace\n\n\342\234\223 Inspect repository\n\342\234\223 Search relevant files\n\342\234\223 Read 11 files\n\342\234\223 Determine ownership\n\n\342\227\217 Plan\n  1. modify composer layout\n  2. run frontend tests\n  3. build\n  4. visually verify\n\n\342\234\223 Edit 3 files\n\342\234\223 Tests 18/18\n\342\234\223 Build successful\n\n\342\227\217 Browser verification\n\342\234\223 Open preview\n\342\234\223 Check mobile viewport\n\342\234\223 Inspect console\n\342\234\223 Capture screenshot\n\n\342\234\223 Git diff reviewed\n\nReady to commit\n\nExactly like the Antigravity execution ledger you were admiring.\n\nHow quickly?\n\nGiven what already exists in your repo, I wouldn\'t treat this as a month-long AgentSam rebuild.\n\nA realistic first dogfood target is roughly:\n\nSlice\tEstimate\nThink/Agent mission shell + AI Gateway route\t1\342\200\2232 hr\nAgentSam execution adapter + Computer experiment\t2\342\200\2233 hr\nCode Mode over existing filesystem/Git tools\t2\342\200\2234 hr\nExisting Browser lane \342\206\222 verifier\t2\342\200\2233 hr\nexecution ledger in existing Workbench\t2\342\200\2234 hr\nrun one real InnerAnimalMedia repair end-to-end\tsame day / next day\n\nSo one focused day can plausibly get us a genuinely useful coding-agent vertical slice.\n\nNot \342\200\234replacement for Cursor fully polished.\342\200\235\n\nBut enough that the next InnerAnimalMedia task gets assigned to AgentSam instead of Cursor.\n\nThen every successful mission makes it more useful.\n\nThe stack I\'d bet on\n\nBrain: GLM-5.3 Flash\nHard-task escalation: GLM-5.3\nHarness: @cloudflare/think\nMulti-tool efficiency: Code Mode\nWorkspace experiment: @cloudflare/computer\nProduction Linux execution: Sandbox SDK / Containers\nCheap browser: Kitesurf\nFull browser: Browser Run Chromium\nLong-lived state: Durable Objects\nRare durable job orchestration: Workflows\nProvider/model budget authority: AI Gateway Dynamic Routing + Spend Limits\nExternal interoperability: MCP 2026-07-28\n\nThat feels radically smaller than the AgentSam stack we would have needed even six months ago.\n\nAnd GLM-5.3 Flash at $0.15/M input and $0.50/M output might be the most consequential thing here for getting you off a $200/month IDE agent subscription while still having a model intended for serious agentic coding.\n\nI\'d make the next sprint AgentSam Build Mode v0: no redesign, no new platform hierarchy, no new god router \342\200\224 wire these primitives behind the backend AgentSam boundary and force it to complete one real outstanding InnerAnimalMedia repair from inspect \342\206\222 edit \342\206\222 test \342\206\222 browser verify \342\206\222 commit."
    items {
      text: "add Yeah \342\200\224 I checked Cloudflare\342\200\231s current stack as of today, plus the shape of your current main, and there\342\200\231s a much shorter path than continuing to hand-build every piece of a Cursor replacement.\n\nThe biggest discovery is that Cloudflare has basically converged on the architecture we\342\200\231ve been circling around.\n\nThe new centerpiece: @cloudflare/computer\n\nCloudflare released @cloudflare/computer on August 3 specifically for agents that need to work on real codebases. Their own framing is essentially: an agent needs a computer, not a container.\n\nIt gives an agent:\n\npersistent SQLite-backed filesystem\nread\nwrite\nedit\nls\nexec\nGit/repository operations\nauditing/gating\nmultiple execution backends\n\nAnd the clever part is that not every command spins up Linux.\n\nAgent Sam\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\226\274\nWorkspace / Computer\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Worker isolate\n   \342\224\202     grep\n   \342\224\202     cat\n   \342\224\202     sed\n   \342\224\202     jq\n   \342\224\202     file edits\n   \342\224\202     searches\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Linux container\n         npm install\n         npm test\n         vite build\n         git\n         native binaries\n         long-running server\n\nThe Worker backend uses just-bash + Dynamic Workers for cheap textual work; the container is lazily reached only when a real Linux userland is necessary. One workspace can have both backends simultaneously.\n\nThat is almost exactly the execution router we\'ve been trying to evolve AgentSam toward.\n\nOne caveat: @cloudflare/computer is explicitly preview-only and not recommended as a production dependency yet. So I would put it behind AgentSam\'s execution contract, not make the whole product depend directly on it.\n\nThen Cloudflare quietly solved another huge AgentSam problem: Code Mode\n\nThis one may be even more important for the Cursor replacement.\n\nRight now a traditional agent often does:\n\nmodel\n \342\206\223\nfs_search\n \342\206\223\nmodel\n \342\206\223\nfs_read\n \342\206\223\nmodel\n \342\206\223\nfs_read\n \342\206\223\nmodel\n \342\206\223\ngrep\n \342\206\223\nmodel\n \342\206\223\ngit_diff\n \342\206\223\nmodel\n\nEvery damn little operation creates another model round trip.\n\nCloudflare Code Mode lets the model instead write a small program that composes tools:\n\nconst files = await tools.search(\"resolveIdentity\");\n\nconst relevant = files\n  .filter(...)\n  .slice(0, 20);\n\nconst contents = await Promise.all(\n  relevant.map(f => tools.read(f.path))\n);\n\nreturn analyze(contents);\n\nOne model decision can therefore perform a whole mini-workflow of dependent operations, loops, filtering, branching, and result shaping. Cloudflare specifically recommends it for large tool catalogs and multi-step work.\n\nThat attacks two of AgentSam\'s current problems simultaneously:\n\ntool-call count explosion and huge MCP schema/context overhead.\n\nIt can also expose your existing MCP tools through Code Mode instead of dumping every MCP schema into every turn. Cloudflare added durable MCP Code Mode integration, discovery, approvals and execution history.\n\nThat is the thing I would prioritize.\n\nAnd the model situation just got ridiculous\n\nThis happened basically yesterday.\n\nCloudflare added GLM-5.3, explicitly positioning it as a long-running agentic coding model. It gets a 1,048,576-token context window, function calling, reasoning and structured outputs. Cloudflare cites dramatic improvements over GLM-5.2 on terminal and long-horizon software-engineering benchmarks.\n\nPricing:\n\nGLM-5.3\n\n$1.40 / M input\n$0.26 / M cached input\n$4.40 / M output\n\nBut the one I\'d hit constantly is the new GLM-5.3 Flash.\n\nCloudflare says it outperforms GLM-5.2 across its comparisons while approaching Claude Opus 4.8 on coding/agentic benchmarks, and it has the same 1M context plus vision/function-calling/reasoning.\n\nIts price is:\n\nGLM-5.3 Flash\n\n$0.15 / M input\n$0.03 / M cached input\n$0.50 / M output\n\nThat is the model I would make the AgentSam workhorse.\n\nNot the expensive model.\n\nAgentSam\'s model ladder becomes stupidly simple\n                   AgentSam Mission\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                    AI Gateway\n                         \342\224\202\n             \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n             \342\224\202                      \342\224\202\n             \342\226\274                      \342\226\274\n       GLM-5.3 Flash            GLM-5.3\n        DEFAULT                  ESCALATE\n      $0.15 / M in             $1.40 / M in\n      $0.50 / M out            $4.40 / M out\n             \342\224\202\n             \342\224\202 failure / high complexity\n             \342\226\274\n       provider fallback\n   Gemini / OpenAI / Anthropic\n\nCloudflare AI Gateway can now implement that routing without us hard-coding it into AgentSam.\n\nDynamic Routing supports conditions, model fallbacks, quotas, rate limits, budget limits and versioned routes.\n\nAnd this is especially relevant after burning the Cursor budget:\n\nCloudflare added actual dollar spend limits.\n\nYou can say effectively:\n\nAgentSam\ndaily budget: $5\n\nGLM Flash:\n    normal use\n\nGLM 5.3:\n    maximum $2/day\n\nexpensive external providers:\n    maximum $1/day\n\nbudget exhausted:\n    fall back to cheaper model\n\nAI Gateway will calculate model costs and enforce it, including BYOK requests.\n\nThat should become non-negotiable for AgentSam.\n\nNo more discovering the bill after the agent went wild.\n\nCloudflare also basically built our Browser lane\n\nYou already peeled MYBROWSER into its own backend domain.\n\nGood decision.\n\nCloudflare renamed Browser Rendering \342\206\222 Browser Run, and agents can now control real Chrome through CDP by writing code rather than being limited to a dozen browser_click, browser_navigate, etc. actions.\n\nBut the newest interesting part is Kitesurf.\n\nIt\'s an agent-first browser running in Workers rather than Chromium. Cloudflare says common agent workloads use 3\342\200\2237\303\227 less CPU/memory, and it\'s currently free during beta.\n\nSo MYBROWSER could eventually route:\n\nNeed webpage understanding?\n        \342\224\202\n        \342\226\274\n    Kitesurf\n    cheap / fast\n        \342\224\202\n        \342\224\202 insufficient?\n        \342\226\274\n     Chromium\n    full browser\n\nPerfect for:\n\nchange frontend\n      \342\206\223\ndeploy preview\n      \342\206\223\nopen page\n      \342\206\223\naccessibility tree\n      \342\206\223\ninspect console\n      \342\206\223\nscreenshot\n      \342\206\223\ncompare\n      \342\206\223\nrepair\n\nAnd Browser Run now has structured human handoff and an accessibility-tree endpoint specifically useful to agents.\n\nThat gets us much closer to:\n\n\342\200\234Fix the mobile composer.\342\200\235\n\ninstead of:\n\n\342\200\234write some CSS and tell Sam to see whether it worked.\342\200\235\n\nThe actual AgentSam I\'d build now\n\nNot another architecture rewrite.\n\nThis:\n\n                    AGENTSAM\n                       \342\224\202\n                       \342\226\274\n              @cloudflare/think\n         session / streaming / memory\n                       \342\224\202\n                       \342\226\274\n                 runTurn()\n                       \342\224\202\n             \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n             \342\224\202                   \342\224\202\n        direct tools         Code Mode\n        simple action       multi-tool plan\n             \342\224\202                   \342\224\202\n             \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                       \342\226\274\n             AgentSam Workspace\n                       \342\224\202\n        \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\274\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n        \342\224\202              \342\224\202               \342\224\202\n        \342\226\274              \342\226\274               \342\226\274\n    Computer       Sandbox          Local Mac\n    Worker         Container        localpty\n    isolate          Linux\n        \342\224\202              \342\224\202\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                \342\224\202\n                \342\226\274\n            repository\n                \342\224\202\n        \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n        \342\226\274                \342\226\274\n     Git/GitHub       Browser Run\n                         \342\224\202\n                   Kitesurf / Chrome\n\n@cloudflare/think is now a pretty serious harness itself: durable-object state, persisted messages, streaming, resumability, agentic tool loops, client tools and sub-agents.\n\nCloudflare also added detached background sub-agents with durable progress and milestones, which survive disconnects/evictions.\n\nSo a build mission could become:\n\nMISSION\nRepair mobile chat composer\n       \342\224\202\n       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Inspector\n       \342\224\202     repo search\n       \342\224\202\n       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Builder\n       \342\224\202     edits + tests\n       \342\224\202\n       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Browser verifier\n             live page + screenshot\n\nwhile the parent AgentSam remains responsive.\n\nDon\'t put Workflows everywhere\n\nThis is important given all the overlap we\'ve been ripping out.\n\nUse:\n\nAgent/DO\nfor interactive mission state.\n\nCode Mode\nfor a burst of related tool operations.\n\nComputer/Sandbox\nfor execution.\n\nDetached sub-agent\nfor another intelligent worker.\n\nWorkflow\nonly when execution genuinely needs durable sleeps/retries/checkpoints across long periods.\n\nCloudflare themselves describe Agents as real-time state/communication and Workflows as durable execution.\n\nSo don\'t create:\n\nAgent\n \342\206\222 Workflow\n   \342\206\222 Queue\n     \342\206\222 Agent\n       \342\206\222 Workflow\n         \342\206\222 Container\n\nfor every shell command.\n\nThat\'s exactly the infrastructure lasagna you\'ve been trying to delete.\n\nI checked current main, too\n\nYou\'re much closer than starting over.\n\nThe current tree already has:\n\napp/agentsam/frontend/workbench/browser/\nbackend/\ncontainers/\nagentsam-sdk/\n\nand a substantial browser workbench already exists.\n\nInterestingly, when I searched main for the actual new Cloudflare runtime imports, I found the Agents/Sandbox material primarily in your .cursor/rules/cloudflare-*.mdc documentation rather than the application runtime itself.\n\nSo we haven\'t missed some giant finished integration.\n\nThere is a clean opportunity to introduce this behind the backend AgentSam boundary without ripping up the frontend again.\n\nI would not port that Antigravity Python demo wholesale.\n\nThe first vertical slice\n\nI would make exactly one thing work:\n\nAgentSam receives an InnerAnimalMedia engineering mission and finishes it.\n\nSomething like:\n\nFix the mobile chat composer.\nInspect existing implementation first.\nDo not create duplicate ownership.\nRun relevant tests.\nOpen the production/preview UI.\nVerify the repair visually.\nCommit only after verification.\n\nAnd AgentSam should visibly do:\n\n\342\227\217 Preparing workspace\n\n\342\234\223 Inspect repository\n\342\234\223 Search relevant files\n\342\234\223 Read 11 files\n\342\234\223 Determine ownership\n\n\342\227\217 Plan\n  1. modify composer layout\n  2. run frontend tests\n  3. build\n  4. visually verify\n\n\342\234\223 Edit 3 files\n\342\234\223 Tests 18/18\n\342\234\223 Build successful\n\n\342\227\217 Browser verification\n\342\234\223 Open preview\n\342\234\223 Check mobile viewport\n\342\234\223 Inspect console\n\342\234\223 Capture screenshot\n\n\342\234\223 Git diff reviewed\n\nReady to commit\n\nExactly like the Antigravity execution ledger you were admiring.\n\nHow quickly?\n\nGiven what already exists in your repo, I wouldn\'t treat this as a month-long AgentSam rebuild.\n\nA realistic first dogfood target is roughly:\n\nSlice\tEstimate\nThink/Agent mission shell + AI Gateway route\t1\342\200\2232 hr\nAgentSam execution adapter + Computer experiment\t2\342\200\2233 hr\nCode Mode over existing filesystem/Git tools\t2\342\200\2234 hr\nExisting Browser lane \342\206\222 verifier\t2\342\200\2233 hr\nexecution ledger in existing Workbench\t2\342\200\2234 hr\nrun one real InnerAnimalMedia repair end-to-end\tsame day / next day\n\nSo one focused day can plausibly get us a genuinely useful coding-agent vertical slice.\n\nNot \342\200\234replacement for Cursor fully polished.\342\200\235\n\nBut enough that the next InnerAnimalMedia task gets assigned to AgentSam instead of Cursor.\n\nThen every successful mission makes it more useful.\n\nThe stack I\'d bet on\n\nBrain: GLM-5.3 Flash\nHard-task escalation: GLM-5.3\nHarness: @cloudflare/think\nMulti-tool efficiency: Code Mode\nWorkspace experiment: @cloudflare/computer\nProduction Linux execution: Sandbox SDK / Containers\nCheap browser: Kitesurf\nFull browser: Browser Run Chromium\nLong-lived state: Durable Objects\nRare durable job orchestration: Workflows\nProvider/model budget authority: AI Gateway Dynamic Routing + Spend Limits\nExternal interoperability: MCP 2026-07-28\n\nThat feels radically smaller than the AgentSam stack we would have needed even six months ago.\n\nAnd GLM-5.3 Flash at $0.15/M input and $0.50/M output might be the most consequential thing here for getting you off a $200/month IDE agent subscription while still having a model intended for serious agentic coding.\n\nI\'d make the next sprint AgentSam Build Mode v0: no redesign, no new platform hierarchy, no new god router \342\200\224 wire these primitives behind the backend AgentSam boundary and force it to complete one real outstanding InnerAnimalMedia repair from inspect \342\206\222 edit \342\206\222 test \342\206\222 browser verify \342\206\222 commit."
    }
  }
}
