steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787971113
      nanos: 15478101
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "give it this. I\342\200\231d make Bindings a first-class settings tab and use Monaco as an actual configuration/code surface, not just decoration.\n\nExtend the current AgentSamRemix app with a production-quality Cloudflare Bindings + Code Editor capability. Preserve the existing UI language and do not redesign the app.\n\nFirst inspect the current project structure, package.json, settings implementation, types, and state flow. Reuse existing primitives and ownership. Do not create duplicate settings systems.\n\n1. Add a Bindings settings surface\n\nAdd a new tab inside the existing App Settings & Live Theme Engine:\n\nBindings & Runtime\n\nThis should configure the bindings available to an AgentSam/Cloudflare Worker environment.\n\nSupport these binding families:\n\nD1 databases\nKV namespaces\nR2 buckets\nDurable Objects\nWorkers AI\nBrowser / Browser Run\nVectorize\nQueues\nWorkflows\nService bindings\nAnalytics Engine\nEnvironment variables\nSecrets / secret references\n\nDo not treat secrets as normal plaintext config values.\n\nEach binding should have a compact row/card showing:\n\nbinding variable name\nbinding type\nresource name/id where applicable\nenvironment\nstatus\nedit/remove controls\n\nExample:\n\nDB              D1             inneranimalmedia-business    Connected\nCACHE           KV             SESSION_CACHE                Connected\nSTORAGE         R2             agentsam-artifacts           Connected\nAI              Workers AI                                 Available\nBROWSER         Browser Run                                Available\nAGENT_SESSION   Durable Object AgentChatSqlV1              Bound\n\nAdd + Add Binding with a clean type picker and only show the fields relevant to the selected binding.\n\nKeep this surface quiet and compact. Use progressive disclosure rather than a giant infrastructure form.\n\n2. Binding configuration model\n\nIntroduce a typed internal binding schema instead of scattering binding-specific fields through UI components.\n\nConceptually:\n\ntype RuntimeBinding =\n  | D1Binding\n  | KVBinding\n  | R2Binding\n  | DurableObjectBinding\n  | WorkersAIBinding\n  | BrowserBinding\n  | VectorizeBinding\n  | QueueBinding\n  | WorkflowBinding\n  | ServiceBinding\n  | AnalyticsBinding\n  | VariableBinding\n  | SecretBinding;\n\nKeep parsing, validation, serialization, UI, and runtime ownership separated.\n\n3. Wrangler config import/export\n\nAdd support for viewing/editing the Cloudflare configuration representation.\n\nSupport the project\'s actual format after inspecting it:\n\nwrangler.jsonc\nwrangler.toml\nor equivalent current config\n\nProvide:\n\nVisual | Code\n\nThe visual binding editor and raw config editor should represent the same underlying state, not two disconnected configurations.\n\nChanges in either view should be reflected in the other after validation.\n\n4. Install Monaco Editor\n\nAdd Monaco as the reusable application code editor.\n\nInspect the current frontend stack first and use the cleanest compatible Monaco integration. For a React app, prefer a maintained React integration around Monaco rather than manually wiring the entire editor runtime unless there is a reason not to.\n\nInstall the required package(s), update package configuration correctly, and verify the production build.\n\nBuild a reusable component such as:\n\ncomponents/editor/\n  MonacoEditor.tsx\n  editorTypes.ts\n  editorTheme.ts\n\nDo not couple Monaco directly to the bindings feature.\n\nWe will reuse this editor elsewhere in AgentSam.\n\n5. Monaco capabilities\n\nInitially support:\n\nTypeScript\nJavaScript\nJSON\nJSONC\nMarkdown\nCSS\nHTML\nYAML if supported cleanly\nshell\n\nInclude:\n\nsyntax highlighting\nline numbers\nfind\nkeyboard shortcuts\nminimap toggle\nword wrap\nread-only mode\ndirty-state indicator\nvalidation/error markers where practical\nlight/dark theme compatibility with the live theme engine\n\nMonaco should visually inherit the current app theme rather than looking like a foreign VS Code iframe.\n\n6. Add a real Code workspace\n\nThe app already exposes Preview / Code.\n\nUpgrade Code into a useful lightweight workspace using Monaco.\n\nLayout:\n\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202 File tree    \342\224\202 Monaco                              \342\224\202\n\342\224\202              \342\224\202                                     \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 app/         \342\224\202 selected file contents              \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 backend/     \342\224\202                                     \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 config/      \342\224\202                                     \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n\nInclude:\n\nfile tree\nopen-file tabs\nactive/dirty state\nsave\nread-only support\nunsaved change protection\n\nReuse the current runtime/filesystem abstraction. Do not create a fake filesystem specifically for Monaco.\n\n7. Bindings + Monaco integration\n\nInside Bindings & Runtime, add:\n\nVisual Config | Raw Config\n\nRaw Config opens the relevant Wrangler configuration in Monaco.\n\nWhen the user edits raw binding configuration:\n\nparse it\nvalidate it\nshow Monaco diagnostics for invalid configuration\npreview the resulting binding changes\nrequire an explicit Apply/Save action\n\nDo not silently overwrite working configuration.\n\n8. Runtime environment awareness\n\nBindings should be associated with an execution environment.\n\nPrepare the model for:\n\nLocal\nCloudflare Worker\nCloudflare Sandbox / Container\nGoogle AntiGravity\nRemote VM\n\nNot every environment supports every binding.\n\nShow unsupported bindings as unavailable rather than pretending they work.\n\n9. UX\n\nPreserve the clean interaction style already established.\n\nI want:\n\none coherent settings modal\ncompact tabs\nrestrained controls\nimmediate feedback\nno huge infrastructure dashboard\nadvanced details hidden until requested\n\nA user should be able to understand:\n\n\342\200\234These are the resources this AgentSam environment can access.\342\200\235\n\nwithout needing to understand Cloudflare\'s entire platform.\n\n10. Verification\n\nAfter implementation:\n\ninstall dependencies\nrun typecheck\nrun tests\nrun production build\nopen the live preview\nverify Monaco renders\nverify Preview \342\206\224 Code switching\nverify at least D1, KV, R2, Durable Object and Workers AI bindings can be represented\nverify raw config parsing\nverify invalid configuration produces diagnostics instead of corrupting state\n\nDo not stop at scaffolding. Build the functional vertical slice and show me the working UI.\n\nOne extra thing I\342\200\231d add as a final sentence because it\342\200\231ll keep Google from inventing another pile of architecture:\n\nUse this as the beginning of AgentSam\'s actual reusable code workspace. Do not create a separate \342\200\234Bindings app,\342\200\235 separate editor application, or parallel configuration authority.\n\nThat last constraint matters a lot. Monaco + file tree + Preview is basically the start of the Cursor-shaped capability we actually need, while Bindings becomes part of the environment rather than another settings rabbit hole."
    items {
      text: "give it this. I\342\200\231d make Bindings a first-class settings tab and use Monaco as an actual configuration/code surface, not just decoration.\n\nExtend the current AgentSamRemix app with a production-quality Cloudflare Bindings + Code Editor capability. Preserve the existing UI language and do not redesign the app.\n\nFirst inspect the current project structure, package.json, settings implementation, types, and state flow. Reuse existing primitives and ownership. Do not create duplicate settings systems.\n\n1. Add a Bindings settings surface\n\nAdd a new tab inside the existing App Settings & Live Theme Engine:\n\nBindings & Runtime\n\nThis should configure the bindings available to an AgentSam/Cloudflare Worker environment.\n\nSupport these binding families:\n\nD1 databases\nKV namespaces\nR2 buckets\nDurable Objects\nWorkers AI\nBrowser / Browser Run\nVectorize\nQueues\nWorkflows\nService bindings\nAnalytics Engine\nEnvironment variables\nSecrets / secret references\n\nDo not treat secrets as normal plaintext config values.\n\nEach binding should have a compact row/card showing:\n\nbinding variable name\nbinding type\nresource name/id where applicable\nenvironment\nstatus\nedit/remove controls\n\nExample:\n\nDB              D1             inneranimalmedia-business    Connected\nCACHE           KV             SESSION_CACHE                Connected\nSTORAGE         R2             agentsam-artifacts           Connected\nAI              Workers AI                                 Available\nBROWSER         Browser Run                                Available\nAGENT_SESSION   Durable Object AgentChatSqlV1              Bound\n\nAdd + Add Binding with a clean type picker and only show the fields relevant to the selected binding.\n\nKeep this surface quiet and compact. Use progressive disclosure rather than a giant infrastructure form.\n\n2. Binding configuration model\n\nIntroduce a typed internal binding schema instead of scattering binding-specific fields through UI components.\n\nConceptually:\n\ntype RuntimeBinding =\n  | D1Binding\n  | KVBinding\n  | R2Binding\n  | DurableObjectBinding\n  | WorkersAIBinding\n  | BrowserBinding\n  | VectorizeBinding\n  | QueueBinding\n  | WorkflowBinding\n  | ServiceBinding\n  | AnalyticsBinding\n  | VariableBinding\n  | SecretBinding;\n\nKeep parsing, validation, serialization, UI, and runtime ownership separated.\n\n3. Wrangler config import/export\n\nAdd support for viewing/editing the Cloudflare configuration representation.\n\nSupport the project\'s actual format after inspecting it:\n\nwrangler.jsonc\nwrangler.toml\nor equivalent current config\n\nProvide:\n\nVisual | Code\n\nThe visual binding editor and raw config editor should represent the same underlying state, not two disconnected configurations.\n\nChanges in either view should be reflected in the other after validation.\n\n4. Install Monaco Editor\n\nAdd Monaco as the reusable application code editor.\n\nInspect the current frontend stack first and use the cleanest compatible Monaco integration. For a React app, prefer a maintained React integration around Monaco rather than manually wiring the entire editor runtime unless there is a reason not to.\n\nInstall the required package(s), update package configuration correctly, and verify the production build.\n\nBuild a reusable component such as:\n\ncomponents/editor/\n  MonacoEditor.tsx\n  editorTypes.ts\n  editorTheme.ts\n\nDo not couple Monaco directly to the bindings feature.\n\nWe will reuse this editor elsewhere in AgentSam.\n\n5. Monaco capabilities\n\nInitially support:\n\nTypeScript\nJavaScript\nJSON\nJSONC\nMarkdown\nCSS\nHTML\nYAML if supported cleanly\nshell\n\nInclude:\n\nsyntax highlighting\nline numbers\nfind\nkeyboard shortcuts\nminimap toggle\nword wrap\nread-only mode\ndirty-state indicator\nvalidation/error markers where practical\nlight/dark theme compatibility with the live theme engine\n\nMonaco should visually inherit the current app theme rather than looking like a foreign VS Code iframe.\n\n6. Add a real Code workspace\n\nThe app already exposes Preview / Code.\n\nUpgrade Code into a useful lightweight workspace using Monaco.\n\nLayout:\n\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202 File tree    \342\224\202 Monaco                              \342\224\202\n\342\224\202              \342\224\202                                     \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 app/         \342\224\202 selected file contents              \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 backend/     \342\224\202                                     \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 config/      \342\224\202                                     \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n\nInclude:\n\nfile tree\nopen-file tabs\nactive/dirty state\nsave\nread-only support\nunsaved change protection\n\nReuse the current runtime/filesystem abstraction. Do not create a fake filesystem specifically for Monaco.\n\n7. Bindings + Monaco integration\n\nInside Bindings & Runtime, add:\n\nVisual Config | Raw Config\n\nRaw Config opens the relevant Wrangler configuration in Monaco.\n\nWhen the user edits raw binding configuration:\n\nparse it\nvalidate it\nshow Monaco diagnostics for invalid configuration\npreview the resulting binding changes\nrequire an explicit Apply/Save action\n\nDo not silently overwrite working configuration.\n\n8. Runtime environment awareness\n\nBindings should be associated with an execution environment.\n\nPrepare the model for:\n\nLocal\nCloudflare Worker\nCloudflare Sandbox / Container\nGoogle AntiGravity\nRemote VM\n\nNot every environment supports every binding.\n\nShow unsupported bindings as unavailable rather than pretending they work.\n\n9. UX\n\nPreserve the clean interaction style already established.\n\nI want:\n\none coherent settings modal\ncompact tabs\nrestrained controls\nimmediate feedback\nno huge infrastructure dashboard\nadvanced details hidden until requested\n\nA user should be able to understand:\n\n\342\200\234These are the resources this AgentSam environment can access.\342\200\235\n\nwithout needing to understand Cloudflare\'s entire platform.\n\n10. Verification\n\nAfter implementation:\n\ninstall dependencies\nrun typecheck\nrun tests\nrun production build\nopen the live preview\nverify Monaco renders\nverify Preview \342\206\224 Code switching\nverify at least D1, KV, R2, Durable Object and Workers AI bindings can be represented\nverify raw config parsing\nverify invalid configuration produces diagnostics instead of corrupting state\n\nDo not stop at scaffolding. Build the functional vertical slice and show me the working UI.\n\nOne extra thing I\342\200\231d add as a final sentence because it\342\200\231ll keep Google from inventing another pile of architecture:\n\nUse this as the beginning of AgentSam\'s actual reusable code workspace. Do not create a separate \342\200\234Bindings app,\342\200\235 separate editor application, or parallel configuration authority.\n\nThat last constraint matters a lot. Monaco + file tree + Preview is basically the start of the Cursor-shaped capability we actually need, while Bindings becomes part of the environment rather than another settings rabbit hole."
    }
  }
}
