    thinking: "**Reviewing User Requests**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user\'s prompt to understand the specific requirements, specifically focusing on the requested \"Bindings\" settings surface. It looks like I need to implement a new tab within the existing \"App Settings & Live Theme Engine\" structure. This is a good starting point for detailed planning.\n\n\n**Defining Binding Capabilities**\n\nI\'ve scoped out the \"Bindings & Runtime\" tab, which is taking shape in `AppSettingsModal.tsx`. It\'ll handle AgentSam and Cloudflare Worker binding configuration, including diverse binding families. I\'m focusing on features such as masked secret display, and the detailed properties each binding needs, including environment-specific overrides, descriptions, and status indicators.\n\n\n**Implementing Editor Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating a Monaco Editor within the Bindings tab, enabling \"Raw\" view. I\'m focusing on two-way synchronization between visual and raw configurations, ensuring error handling for invalid JSON/JSONC/TOML changes. I\'m creating reusable editor components within `components/editor/` to maintain a consistent style.\n\n\n**Expanding Code Workspace**\n\nI\'m now focusing on upgrading the \"Code\" view into a full workspace. This involves adding features such as a file explorer for navigating files like `wrangler.jsonc`, `src/index.ts`, and `package.json`. I\'m also implementing multi-tab file switching with a dirty indicator, and close buttons, along with diff viewer capabilities. This workspace integration is for both the main app environment and the browser code view. I need to make the Code tab a truly productive environment. I plan to handle syntax highlighting for TypeScript, JavaScript, JSON, and other formats.\n\n\n"
