    thinking: "**Defining Binding Schema**\n\nI\'m currently focused on systematically defining the typed internal binding schema. My priority is supporting all requested Cloudflare Worker runtime binding families within `types/bindings.ts`, specifically focusing on `d1` and its nuances like `binding`, `database_name`, and `database_id`. I\'m aiming for a comprehensive and organized structure.\n\n\n**Expanding Binding Coverage**\n\nI\'ve expanded the schema to cover a broader range of binding families. Now, I\'m integrating KV Namespace, R2 Bucket, Durable Objects, Workers AI, Browser, Vectorize Index, Queues, Workflows, Service Bindings, Analytics Engine, and environment variables and secrets. Each binding has an ID, a family, and the binding name, the essential structure for consistent application. I will be incorporating this into a standardized typed format.\n\n\n**Adding Binding Attributes**\n\nI\'m now incorporating attributes like `enabled`, `environment`, and `description` to each binding. I\'m focusing on accurately representing binding `status` as `\'configured\'`, `\'bound\'`, etc. Also, an optional `isSecret` flag is being included, along with family-specific configurations. The goal is a more detailed representation.\n\nI\'m also working on preset templates for common use cases, such as an \"AgentSam Complete AI Stack\" and \"Full-Stack SQLite + Vectorize + AI\". I am designing converters to transition bindings into a usable `wrangler.jsonc` format. The converter will also robustly parse binding types back from JSON to a typed format.\n\n\n**Integrating Editor Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Monaco Editor improvements. I\'ve defined editor types and themes, which are dynamically synced with the application\'s theme, including custom themes. I\'m focusing on features such as loading states, custom theme definitions, toggling readOnly modes, line numbers, and keyboard shortcuts. Also, I\'m integrating the Monaco Diff Editor for side-by-side comparisons of code changes. This is important for version control and AI-driven edits.\n\n\n\n**Developing Binding Runtime View**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the new \"Bindings & Runtime\" tab within the settings modal. This will offer both a visual and raw (JSONC) representation of bindings, with instant, bi-directional sync. The visual view will include filterable binding cards, each with status indicators and editable fields, and the raw view will use a live Monaco editor with validation and formatting. I\'m also adding an \"Add Binding\" modal with presets.\n\n\n**Displaying Backend Compatibility**\n\nI\'m now integrating compatibility information for the active backend, detailing how bindings execute across Worker isolates, containers, and sandboxes within the \"Bindings & Runtime\" tab. Additionally, I am including quick \"Sync to Visual\" buttons with validation feedback to streamline the binding process. I\'m focused on a clear, understandable representation of the execution environment.\n\nI\'m also working on upgrading the \"Code\" Workspace. A dedicated Code Workspace tab has been implemented in `AgentSamEnvironment.tsx` with a File Explorer / Tree Sidebar and the ability to add new files. Rich project files will be accessible including `wrangler.jsonc` (live bound to the Bindings store!), `src/index.ts`, `src/agent.ts`, and `src/tools.ts`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 37183504
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
