    user_response: "make every operation require knowledge of the frontend.\n\n4. Mission runtime\n\nThe SDK should own a real mission lifecycle:\n\ncreated\npreparing\ninspecting\nplanning\nexecuting\nverifying\nreview_ready\ncompleted\nfailed\ncancelled\n\nA mission can execute many tool calls.\n\nDo not assume serious engineering work ends after 3\342\200\2235 operations.\n\nSupport the loop:\n\ninspect\n  \342\206\223\nreason\n  \342\206\223\nact\n  \342\206\223\nobserve\n  \342\206\223\nadjust\n  \342\206\223\nverify\n\nThe current UI execution ledger must consume SDK events rather than maintaining an independent fake lifecycle.\n\n5. Typed execution events\n\nCreate a shared event contract.\n\nExample event families:\n\nenvironment.preparing\nenvironment.ready\n\nmission.started\nmission.plan.updated\n\nrepository.search\nrepository.read\n\ntool.started\ntool.completed\ntool.failed\n\nfile.edited\n\nterminal.started\nterminal.output\nterminal.completed\n\ntest.started\ntest.completed\n\nbrowser.started\nbrowser.verified\n\nartifact.created\n\nverification.started\nverification.passed\nverification.failed\n\nmission.completed\n\nThese events should drive the calm expandable execution UI we\'ve already established.\n\nDefault view = compact.\n\nClick event = reveal details.\n\n6. Execution environments\n\nMake execution backends pluggable.\n\nDefine a common SDK contract capable of representing:\n\nLocal\nCloudflare Computer\nCloudflare Sandbox / Container\nRemote VM\nGoogle AntiGravity\n\nConceptually:\n\ninterface ExecutionEnvironment {\n  id: string;\n  kind: string;\n  prepare(): Promise<void>;\n  exec(...): Promise<ExecutionResult>;\n  readFile(...): Promise<string>;\n  writeFile(...): Promise<void>;\n  capabilities(): Promise<Capability[]>;\n  dispose?(): Promise<void>;\n}\n\nAdapt signatures properly after examining the current application.\n\nThe mission layer must not care whether execution occurs locally, on Cloudflare, or in AntiGravity.\n\n7. Repository intelligence as SDK capability\n\nMove repository intelligence into the SDK.\n\nExpose primitives for:\n\nwalk repository\ninventory files\nlanguage distribution\nLOC\nlarge files\ndirectory density\ndependency pressure\nimport relationships\nGit churn\nfrequently changed files\nstale files\nownership boundaries\nlikely god files\nduplicate authority signals\ntests\nbuild system\npackage/workspace topology\n\nThe result should be machine-readable.\n\nExample:\n\nconst report = await sam.repository.inspect(repo);\n\nUI rendering is separate from analysis.\n\n8. Tool registry\n\nMake tools first-class SDK capabilities.\n\nEach tool should have metadata such as:\n\n{\n  key,\n  title,\n  description,\n  capabilities,\n  risk,\n  environmentRequirements,\n  inputSchema,\n  outputSchema\n}\n\nSupport:\n\nfilesystem\nterminal\nGit\nGitHub\nBrowser\nHTTP\ndatabase\nCloudflare\nartifacts\nsearch\nMCP\n\nDo not hardwire every tool into the orchestrator.\n\n9. Code Mode / tool composition\n\nProvide a higher-order execution API so one reasoning step can compose multiple primitive operations without requiring a model round trip after every filesystem call.\n\nFor example:\n\nawait sam.runCode(async tools => {\n  const matches = await tools.fs.search(\"resolveIdentity\");\n\n  const files = await Promise.all(\n    matches.map(x => tools.fs.read(x.path))\n  );\n\n  return summarize(files);\n});\n\nKeep primitive tools individually callable too.\n\n10. SELF-HOSTING MODE\n\nThis is the most important feature.\n\nAdd an explicit mode:\n\nDevelop AgentSam\n\nIn this mode, AgentSam targets its own SDK/application repository.\n\nExample:\n\nMission:\n\nImprove the AgentSam repository inspector so it identifies\nunusually high Git churn without scanning generated files.\n\nAgentSam should:\n\nPreparing workspace\n\342\206\223\nInspect SDK\n\342\206\223\nLocate repository inspector\n\342\206\223\nUnderstand current implementation\n\342\206\223\nCreate branch\n\342\206\223\nModify SDK using SDK filesystem APIs\n\342\206\223\nRun SDK tests\n\342\206\223\nBenchmark old vs new behavior\n\342\206\223\nInspect diff\n\342\206\223\nRun SDK build/typecheck\n\342\206\223\nVerify no public contract regression\n\342\206\223\nProduce report\n\342\206\223\nReady for review\n\nThis must be real dogfooding.\n\nThe application should not secretly bypass the AgentSam SDK when editing the AgentSam SDK.\n\n11. Bootstrap problem\n\nHandle self-hosting carefully.\n\nThe currently running SDK version is:\n\nSDK N\n\nIt creates and tests:\n\nSDK N+1 candidate\n\nSDK N+1 does not replace SDK N during the mission.\n\nInstead:\n\nrunning SDK N\n      \342\224\202\n      \342\226\274\ncandidate workspace\n      \342\224\202\n      \342\226\274\nSDK N+1\n      \342\224\202\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 typecheck\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 unit tests\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 integration tests\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 mission tests\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 benchmark\n      \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 verification\n              \342\224\202\n              \342\226\274\n         review / merge\n\nOnly a subsequent clean run should load the newly accepted SDK.\n\nNever hot-swap an unverified SDK underneath an active mission.\n\n12. Evolution manifest\n\nEvery self-improvement mission should produce an artifact describing:\n\nobjective\nhypothesis\nfiles changed\npublic contracts affected\ntests added\ntests passed\nbenchmarks before\nbenchmarks after\nmodel/token usage\ntool calls\nexecution duration\nregressions\nunresolved concerns\n\nCall this something clean such as:\n\nEvolution Report\n\nDo not create a giant new subsystem just for the name.\n\n13. Regression gates\n\nAgentSam may propose changes to itself freely inside its isolated branch/workspace, but promotion requires gates.\n\nAt minimum:\n\ntypecheck\nSDK unit tests\nintegration tests\npublic API contract tests\nbuild\nlint where configured\nGit diff review\nno accidental secrets\nno unauthorized destructive action\n\nAlso add a small set of self-hosting missions as regression tests.\n\nExample:\n\ninspect this fixture repository\nfind all imports of X\nedit a file\nrun tests\ngenerate diff\nproduce artifact\n\nIf a candidate SDK cannot perform the core AgentSam workflow, it cannot promote.\n\n14. Branch-based autonomy\n\nAgentSam should never autonomously modify the protected production branch.\n\nSelf-evolution should normally operate as:\n\nmain\n \342\224\202\n \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 agentsam/evolve-<mission>\n           \342\224\202\n           \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 inspect\n           \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 edit\n           \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 test\n           \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 benchmark\n           \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 verify\n                   \342\224\202\n                   \342\226\274\n               review / PR\n\nAllow the user to choose whether the final step is:\n\nleave changes\ncommit\nopen PR\n\nDo not silently merge its own changes.\n\n15. SDK telemetry\n\nBecause AgentSam will improve itself, record enough data to know whether a change actually helped.\n\nTrack:\n\nmission success/failure\nmodel\ntokens\nestimated cost\ntool calls\nretries\nfilesystem reads\nsearches\nedits\ncommands\ntests\nelapsed time\nhuman intervention count\n\nAvoid logging hidden reasoning or secrets.\n\nThe important metric is:\n\nsuccessful mission cost and completion quality, not merely number of tool calls.\n\n16. Monaco integration\n\nThe Monaco workspace being built now should consume the SDK filesystem APIs.\n\nIt should let me inspect what AgentSam is changing while a self-hosting mission runs.\n\nI want:\n\nAgent activity     SDK source\n     \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n     \342\224\202                 \342\226\274\n     \342\224\202              Monaco\n     \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n     \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 live diff\n\nDo not create an unrelated second editor.\n\n17. Preview / Code / Changes\n\nPreserve the small product model:\n\nPreview\nCode\nChanges\nArtifacts\n\nFor an SDK mission:\n\nCode = source being modified\n\nChanges = Git diff\n\nArtifacts = Evolution Report, architecture SVG, benchmark results\n\nPreview = app/browser verification when the SDK change affects visible behavior\n\n18. SDK documentation\n\nGenerate useful developer documentation:\n\nGetting Started\nAgentSam Client\nMissions\nEnvironments\nRepository API\nFilesystem API\nTerminal API\nGit API\nBrowser API\nTool Registry\nEvents\nSelf-Hosting\nSafety Model\n\nDocumentation must be generated from actual implemented contracts rather than aspirational APIs that do not exist.\n\n19. CLI\n\nAdd a minimal SDK CLI if the architecture supports it cleanly.\n\nTarget experience:\n\nagentsam inspect .\n\nagentsam mission \\\n  --repo . \\\n  \"find and repair the failing tests\"\n\nagentsam evolve \\\n  \"improve repository search performance\"\n\nThe CLI should call the same SDK as the application.\n\nDo not implement a parallel orchestration engine for the CLI.\n\n20. First self-hosting mission\n\nAfter the SDK vertical slice works, use AgentSam itself to perform one real improvement to the AgentSam SDK.\n\nChoose a small but meaningful task discovered through inspection.\n\nDo not fake the self-hosting demonstration.\n\nI want to watch:\n\nAgentSam SDK\n      \342\206\223\nopens AgentSam SDK\n      \342\206\223\ndiagnoses a real limitation\n      \342\206\223\nchanges AgentSam SDK\n      \342\206\223\ntests AgentSam SDK\n      \342\206\223\ncompares results\n      \342\206\223\npresents the change\n\nShow the complete execution ledger.\n\nProduct principle\n\nAgentSam should become the best tool for developing AgentSam.\n\nEvery infrastructure capability exposed to applications should eventually be usable by AgentSam itself.\n\nHowever:\n\nself-evolution is software development, not uncontrolled mutation.\n\nCandidate changes happen in isolated workspaces, are measurable, tested, reversible, reviewable, and versioned.\n\nCritical implementation constraint\n\nDo not build a demo SDK that simply wraps fake state.\n\nMove existing functional behavior behind real SDK contracts and make the current application consume those contracts.\n\nPrefer:\n\none implementation\n     \342\206\221\nAgentSam SDK\n  \342\206\221       \342\206\221\nApp      CLI\n\nrather than:\n\nfrontend implementation\nCLI implementation\nSDK implementation\nself-evolution implementation\n\nThere must be one authority for each capability.\n\nVerification before stopping\n\nDo not stop at scaffolding.\n\nDemonstrate:\n\nSDK imports successfully.\nApp uses SDK.\nMonaco reads files through SDK.\nSDK can inspect a repository.\nSDK can execute a mission.\nSDK can edit a file in an isolated workspace.\nSDK can run terminal commands/tests.\nSDK can produce a Git diff.\nSDK emits typed execution events.\nUI streams those events.\nAgentSam can target its own SDK.\nA candidate self-change passes/fails gates correctly.\nEvolution Report is generated.\nProduction build passes.\n\nThen run the first genuine AgentSam develops AgentSam mission and show me the result.\n\nThe recursion is the fun part:\n\n                    YOU\n                     \342\224\202\n                     \342\226\274\n               AgentSam App\n                     \342\224\202\n                     \342\226\274\n               AgentSam SDK N\n                     \342\224\202\n                     \342\226\274\n          \"improve AgentSam SDK\"\n                     \342\224\202\n                     \342\226\274\n              candidate N+1\n             \342\225\261      \342\224\202       \342\225\262\n          tests   benchmark   verify\n             \342\225\262      \342\224\202       \342\225\261\n                     \342\226\274\n                  review\n                     \342\224\202\n                     \342\226\274\n                AgentSam N+1\n\nThat turns the SDK from \342\200\234some utilities AgentSam happens to have\342\200\235 into the kernel of the product.\n\nAnd once it works, you get a pretty wild feedback loop: you notice AgentSam sucks at something \342\206\222 tell AgentSam to improve that part of its SDK \342\206\222 it inspects its own telemetry/code \342\206\222 builds a candidate \342\206\222 benchmarks it \342\206\222 you approve the better version \342\206\222 next mission runs on the improved SDK.\n\nThat is the version of \342\200\234self-evolving\342\200\235 I\342\200\231d actually trust. The direction I\342\200\231d give that agent is: stop treating this as a benchmark/demo shell and turn it into the actual authenticated Agent Sam operator workbench you can use to refactor and build InnerAnimalMedia.\n\nPaste this to the agent as the next master instruction:\n\nMission: turn AgentSamRemix into the real Agent Sam Workbench\n\nThe current interface is no longer a preview/demo. Build it as a standalone production application whose purpose is to let Agent Sam inspect, edit, test, verify, and refactor real repositories \342\200\224 beginning with SamPrimeaux/inneranimalmedia.\n\nThe finished application should feel like an actual developer application when opened directly, not an app embedded inside an AI Studio preview.\n\nPreserve the strongest pieces already built:\n\nEngineering Mission\nModel Ladder / model routing\nexecution environment selection\nExecution Ledger\nMonaco Code Workspace\nBrowser Verifier\nCode Mode / tool composition\nNetwork Allowlist\nArchitecture Report\nBackend Comparison\ntelemetry/cost visibility\n\nBut reorganize them into a coherent Agent Sam Workbench rather than a benchmarking dashboard.\n\n1. Agent Sam SDK is the canonical application contract\n\nDo not invent a second authentication system, user table, session format, OAuth implementation, or Agent Sam tool contract in this app.\n\nThe canonical portable dependency is:\n\n@inneranimalmedia/agentsam-sdk\n\nCurrent development package identity is:\n\n@inneranimalmedia/agentsam-sdk\n2.0.0-alpha.identity.11\n\nIntegrate through its public exports/subpath exports. Do not copy SDK source into this app.\n\nDevelopment may use a local linked checkout of agentsam-sdk; deployment should consume a pinned package version.\n\nThe ownership rule is:\n\nagentsam-sdk\n    \342\224\202\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 identity contracts\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 repository intelligence\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 portable runtime contracts\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 reusable Agent Sam capabilities\n            \342\224\202\n            \342\226\274\nAgent Sam Workbench\n            \342\224\202\n            \342\226\274\nInnerAnimalMedia host adapters / MCP / infrastructure\n\nHost-specific credentials and bindings stay in this application/server environment. Portable logic stays in the SDK.\n\n2. Use the real Agent Sam Identity package\n\nThe SDK already contains:\n\nimport {\n  createIdentityClient,\n  createIdentityService,\n  createCloudflareD1Adapter,\n  handleIdentityWorkerRequest,\n} from \'@inneranimalmedia/agentsam-sdk/identity\';\n\nDo not create fake auth screens backed by localStorage.\n\nUse the SDK Worker identity implementation.\n\nExisting canonical routes are:\n\nPOST /api/auth/login\nPOST /api/auth/signup\nPOST /api/auth/logout\nGET  /api/auth/me\n\nPOST /api/auth/password-reset/request\nPOST /api/auth/password-reset/confirm\n\nGET /api/oauth/iam/start\nGET /api/oauth/iam/callback\n\nGET /api/oauth/google/start\nGET /api/oauth/google/callback\n\nGET /api/oauth/github/start\nGET /api/oauth/github/callback\n\nGET   /api/company\nPATCH /api/company\n\n/auth/login\n/auth/signup\n/auth/reset\n\nThe default OAuth lane is InnerAnimalMedia IAM, using minted:\n\nIAM_CLIENT_ID\nIAM_CLIENT_SECRET\n\nDeveloper Google/GitHub BYOK remains supported when their credential pairs exist.\n\nNever expose client secrets, Cloudflare tokens, MCP credentials, database credentials, or provider secrets to React/Vite/browser code.\n\n3. Make auth a real application boundary\n\nStructure the app so:\n\n/\n  \342\206\223\nauthenticated?\n  \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 no  \342\206\222 /auth/login\n  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 yes \342\206\222 /dashboard/workbench\n\nUse the SDK\'s authenticated /dashboard/* behavior instead of creating another auth guard implementation unless a tiny host adapter is necessary.\n\nThe actual application should live under:\n\n/dashboard/workbench\n\nwith optional child routes:\n\n/dashboard/workbench\n/dashboard/workbench/repositories\n/dashboard/workbench/browser\n/dashboard/workbench/terminal\n/dashboard/workbench/runs\n/dashboard/workbench/architecture\n/dashboard/workbench/settings\n\nA page refresh on any route must preserve authentication and restore the application normally.\n\nGET /api/auth/me is the browser\'s authoritative current-user check.\n\nDo not consider a client-side boolean such as isLoggedIn=true authentication.\n\n4. Cloudflare-native application boundary\n\nBuild this as a real Cloudflare application.\n\nServer/Worker owns:\n\nauthentication\nauthorization\nsecrets\nD1\nKV\nR2\nDurable Objects\nMCP calls\nGitHub calls\nterminal execution\nAgent Sam tool execution\napproval enforcement\ntelemetry writes\nprovider calls\n\nBrowser owns:\n\napplication shell\nMonaco\nmission composition\nvisual tool state\nexecution stream\ndiff presentation\nbrowser preview\napprovals UI\ntelemetry visualization\n\nBrowser code must never directly possess infrastructure credentials.\n\nStart with the bindings already expected by Agent Sam Identity:\n\nDB\nASSETS\nSESSION_CACHE\n\nand support the existing password-reset email integration through:\n\nRESEND_API_KEY\n\nDo not invent binding names for other services merely for visual completeness. Add a binding only when there is an implementation consuming it.\n\n5. This application is an engineering workbench, not another IDE clone\n\nThe central primitive is a Mission.\n\nA mission might be:\n\n\"Finish the InnerAnimalMedia src/ retirement\"\n\n\"Audit authentication overlap and eliminate duplicate authorities\"\n\n\"Repair the mobile chat composer and verify it in Browser Run\"\n\n\"Inspect agentsam-sdk and extract reusable repository tooling\"\n\nA mission becomes:\n\nMission\n  \342\206\223\nrepository context\n  \342\206\223\nAgent Sam plan\n  \342\206\223\ntool execution loop\n  \342\206\223\ncode/files changed\n  \342\206\223\ntests\n  \342\206\223\nbrowser verification\n  \342\206\223\narchitecture / dependency verification\n  \342\206\223\nreviewable diff\n  \342\206\223\ncommit / PR / deploy if approved\n\nThis flow should become the backbone of the UI.\n\nMonaco is a window into the mission, not the product itself.\n\n6. Repository connection\n\nBuild a proper Repository Workspace model.\n\nInitially support:\n\nSamPrimeaux/inneranimalmedia\nSamPrimeaux/agentsam-sdk\n\nbut do not hardcode Agent Sam\'s architecture around those names.\n\nA repository workspace should expose:\n\nrepository\nbranch/ref\nworking tree status\ncurrent mission\nchanged files\nactive files\nrepo intelligence snapshot\nexecution environment\nterminal connection\nbrowser target\nactive run\napprovals\n\nRepository intelligence should come from the SDK\'s new portable:\n\nagentsam_sdk.repository.intelligence\n\nIt already discovers arbitrary repository layouts rather than assuming src/, backend/, etc.\n\nPresent useful evidence such as:\n\nactive file tree\nlanguage mix\nmanifests\ndirectory density\ncurrent churn\nhot files\npressure points\nstability\n\nLater this should accept dependency/entrypoint graph data without redesigning the UI.\n\n7. Execution environments\n\nDo not make Cloudflare vs Google Antigravity the identity of the app.\n\nThose are execution backends.\n\nModel them generically:\n\nExecution Environment\n\nLocal\nRemote\nSandbox\nCloudflare\nGoogle / Antigravity\n\nEvery environment should report a common capability packet:\n\ninterface ExecutionEnvironment {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  status: \'offline\' | \'starting\' | \'ready\' | \'busy\' | \'error\';\n  capabilities: {\n    filesystem: boolean;\n    terminal: boolean;\n    browser: boolean;\n    network: boolean;\n    git: boolean;\n    isolated: boolean;\n  };\n}\n\nThe UI then chooses the appropriate environment without hardwiring mission logic to one provider.\n\nPreserve the nice environment lifecycle concept:\n\nSpinning up environment\342\200\246\nPreparing workspace\342\200\246\nReady\n8. Execution stream should use progressive disclosure\n\nThe default mission view should remain calm.\n\nRepresent activity chronologically:\n\nThought\nInspect repository\n\nRun Command\nnpm test\n\nRead File\nbackend/agentsam/...\n\nEdit File\n...\n\nBrowser Verify\n...\n\nEach execution row is expandable.\n\nCollapsed state:\n\n\342\234\223 Run Command     npm test                 4.8s\n\nExpanded:\n\ncommand\ncwd\nenvironment\nstdout\nstderr\nexit code\nduration\nrelated files\nreceipt/tool-call ID\n\nDo not permanently dump terminal logs into the main experience.\n\n9. Respect Agent Sam safety/execution semantics\n\nRead operations should be the default.\n\nClearly distinguish:\n\nREAD\nWRITE\nEXECUTE\nEXTERNAL EFFECT\nDESTRUCTIVE\n\nAnything requiring approval must visibly pause the mission and ask for approval.\n\nNever fake an approval by continuing locally.\n\nExamples requiring explicit handling:\n\ngit push\nmerge\ndeploy\ndatabase mutation\nsecret change\nproduction write\ndestructive filesystem operation\nexternal message/send\n\nPreserve an execution receipt/audit trail for every meaningful tool operation.\n\n10. Network allowlist\n\nKeep the Network & Allowlist surface, but make it operational rather than decorative.\n\nIt should show:\n\ndomain\nreason\nenvironment\nrequested by\nallowed/blocked\ntemporary/persistent\n\nUse progressive disclosure.\n\nA normal user shouldn\'t have to stare at network policy while coding.\n\n11. Replace benchmark language\n\nRemove copy that makes this look primarily like:\n\n\"telemetry benchmarker\"\n\"Cloudflare vs Google comparison experiment\"\n\nBackend comparison can remain an advanced diagnostics panel.\n\nMain product language should be:\n\nAgent Sam\nEngineering Workbench\nAutonomous software execution\nRepository workspace\nMission\nRun\nVerify\nReview\n\nThe workbench is allowed to benchmark environments internally, but benchmarking is not the product.\n\n12. Real standalone app shell\n\nRemove any visual feeling of:\n\ndemo in a card\ncentered preview canvas\nfake desktop contained inside another desktop\nexcessive permanent borders around the entire application\n\nThe application should occupy the viewport.\n\nDesktop shell:\n\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202 workspace/repo       Agent Sam          run/status \342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\244\n\342\224\202           \342\224\202                                         \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 nav       \342\224\202 current mission/workspace               \342\224\202\n\342\224\202           \342\224\202                                         \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n\nUse the current visual personality \342\200\224 dark engineering surfaces, subtle glass, restrained status colors \342\200\224 but simplify it.\n\nAvoid filling every inch with pills and badges.\n\nImportant state should be visible; implementation trivia should be expandable.\n\n13. Make InnerAnimalMedia the first real proof\n\nThe first production acceptance case is:\n\nauthenticate as an IAM user\n    \342\206\223\nopen SamPrimeaux/inneranimalmedia\n    \342\206\223\ninspect repository\n    \342\206\223\nbegin an engineering mission\n    \342\206\223\nAgent Sam reads relevant files\n    \342\206\223\nexecutes tools over the appropriate environment\n    \342\206\223\nedits repository\n    \342\206\223\nruns tests\n    \342\206\223\nverifies browser behavior\n    \342\206\223\nshows architecture/dependency impact\n    \342\206\223\nproduces reviewable diff\n    \342\206\223\nasks before commit/push/deploy\n\nIf that works, this is an application.\n\nIf we can only click tabs containing simulated data, it is still a prototype.\n\n14. Do not rebuild existing InnerAnimalMedia backend logic inside this app\n\nInnerAnimalMedia already owns the host infrastructure and Agent Sam runtime.\n\nConnect to it through explicit API/MCP/service adapters.\n\nDo not fork:\n\nauthentication authority\ntool catalog authority\ntelemetry authority\nbrowser authority\nterminal authority\nmodel routing authority\nrepository contracts\n\nThis workbench is a client/operator surface plus its thin host Worker.\n\nWe are actively refactoring InnerAnimalMedia to eliminate duplicated authorities. Do not introduce new ones here.\n\n15. Implementation sequence\n\nWork in this order:\n\nConvert preview layout into full standalone application shell.\nInstall/wire Agent Sam SDK.\nWire real SDK Identity Worker routes.\nAdd login/session/logout and authenticated application routing.\nEstablish Repository Workspace contract.\nTurn current Engineering Mission into the primary mission object.\nNormalize execution backend abstraction.\nConnect execution ledger to real tool/run events.\nConnect Monaco to real repository files/diffs.\nConnect Browser Verifier to actual mission verification.\nConnect repository intelligence.\nWire approvals.\nPersist/recover current mission/workspace.\nRemove all mock data that can now be backed by reality.\nAdd production build/deployment config.\n\nDo not rebuild the entire UI before wiring the contracts.\n\nDefinition of done\n\nI should be able to open the deployed application in a normal browser window and:\n\nbe redirected to Agent Sam auth when signed out;\nsign in through real IAM OAuth;\nrestore my session after refresh;\nsee my authenticated identity;\nselect/connect a repository;\nrun repository intelligence;\ncreate a mission;\nwatch real Agent Sam tool execution;\ninspect individual tool receipts;\nopen/edit actual repository files;\nsee an actual diff;\nexecute tests in a selected environment;\nverify the result in the browser;\nstop for approval on meaningful writes;\nrecover the mission after reload;\nand ultimately operate on SamPrimeaux/inneranimalmedia without adding another duplicate backend authority.\n\nDo not optimize for screenshot completeness. Optimize for one completely real vertical slice.\n\nStart by auditing the current generated project against this specification. Preserve working components. Identify mocks and duplicate authorities. Then implement the smallest complete authenticated vertical slice before expanding any secondary feature.\n\nThat gives the AI Studio agent a much better target than \342\200\234make this an actual app.\342\200\235 The key architectural shift is:\n\nCURRENT\nAgentSamRemix\n  = impressive simulated/benchmark workbench\n\nTARGET\nAgent Sam Workbench\n  = authenticated operator client\n       \342\206\223\n    AgentSam SDK\n       \342\206\223\nInnerAnimalMedia / MCP / execution infrastructure\n       \342\206\223\nreal repository\n\nAnd I especially would not have it build a new auth implementation. I checked current agentsam-sdk/main: the SDK Worker router already has real email login/signup/logout/session, password reset, IAM OAuth, Google/GitHub OAuth, company branding, D1-backed identity, and authenticated /dashboard/* routing. The app should consume that authority and fill any missing SDK seam rather than creating AgentSamRemixAuthService.ts or some other future cleanup project."
    items {
      text: "make every operation require knowledge of the frontend.\n\n4. Mission runtime\n\nThe SDK should own a real mission lifecycle:\n\ncreated\npreparing\ninspecting\nplanning\nexecuting\nverifying\nreview_ready\ncompleted\nfailed\ncancelled\n\nA mission can execute many tool calls.\n\nDo not assume serious engineering work ends after 3\342\200\2235 operations.\n\nSupport the loop:\n\ninspect\n  \342\206\223\nreason\n  \342\206\223\nact\n  \342\206\223\nobserve\n  \342\206\223\nadjust\n  \342\206\223\nverify\n\nThe current UI execution ledger must consume SDK events rather than maintaining an independent fake lifecycle.\n\n5. Typed execution events\n\nCreate a shared event contract.\n\nExample event families:\n\nenvironment.preparing\nenvironment.ready\n\nmission.started\nmission.plan.updated\n\nrepository.search\nrepository.read\n\ntool.started\ntool.completed\ntool.failed\n\nfile.edited\n\nterminal.started\nterminal.output\nterminal.completed\n\ntest.started\ntest.completed\n\nbrowser.started\nbrowser.verified\n\nartifact.created\n\nverification.started\nverification.passed\nverification.failed\n\nmission.completed\n\nThese events should drive the calm expandable execution UI we\'ve already established.\n\nDefault view = compact.\n\nClick event = reveal details.\n\n6. Execution environments\n\nMake execution backends pluggable.\n\nDefine a common SDK contract capable of representing:\n\nLocal\nCloudflare Computer\nCloudflare Sandbox / Container\nRemote VM\nGoogle AntiGravity\n\nConceptually:\n\ninterface ExecutionEnvironment {\n  id: string;\n  kind: string;\n  prepare(): Promise<void>;\n  exec(...): Promise<ExecutionResult>;\n  readFile(...): Promise<string>;\n  writeFile(...): Promise<void>;\n  capabilities(): Promise<Capability[]>;\n  dispose?(): Promise<void>;\n}\n\nAdapt signatures properly after examining the current application.\n\nThe mission layer must not care whether execution occurs locally, on Cloudflare, or in AntiGravity.\n\n7. Repository intelligence as SDK capability\n\nMove repository intelligence into the SDK.\n\nExpose primitives for:\n\nwalk repository\ninventory files\nlanguage distribution\nLOC\nlarge files\ndirectory density\ndependency pressure\nimport relationships\nGit churn\nfrequently changed files\nstale files\nownership boundaries\nlikely god files\nduplicate authority signals\ntests\nbuild system\npackage/workspace topology\n\nThe result should be machine-readable.\n\nExample:\n\nconst report = await sam.repository.inspect(repo);\n\nUI rendering is separate from analysis.\n\n8. Tool registry\n\nMake tools first-class SDK capabilities.\n\nEach tool should have metadata such as:\n\n{\n  key,\n  title,\n  description,\n  capabilities,\n  risk,\n  environmentRequirements,\n  inputSchema,\n  outputSchema\n}\n\nSupport:\n\nfilesystem\nterminal\nGit\nGitHub\nBrowser\nHTTP\ndatabase\nCloudflare\nartifacts\nsearch\nMCP\n\nDo not hardwire every tool into the orchestrator.\n\n9. Code Mode / tool composition\n\nProvide a higher-order execution API so one reasoning step can compose multiple primitive operations without requiring a model round trip after every filesystem call.\n\nFor example:\n\nawait sam.runCode(async tools => {\n  const matches = await tools.fs.search(\"resolveIdentity\");\n\n  const files = await Promise.all(\n    matches.map(x => tools.fs.read(x.path))\n  );\n\n  return summarize(files);\n});\n\nKeep primitive tools individually callable too.\n\n10. SELF-HOSTING MODE\n\nThis is the most important feature.\n\nAdd an explicit mode:\n\nDevelop AgentSam\n\nIn this mode, AgentSam targets its own SDK/application repository.\n\nExample:\n\nMission:\n\nImprove the AgentSam repository inspector so it identifies\nunusually high Git churn without scanning generated files.\n\nAgentSam should:\n\nPreparing workspace\n\342\206\223\nInspect SDK\n\342\206\223\nLocate repository inspector\n\342\206\223\nUnderstand current implementation\n\342\206\223\nCreate branch\n\342\206\223\nModify SDK using SDK filesystem APIs\n\342\206\223\nRun SDK tests\n\342\206\223\nBenchmark old vs new behavior\n\342\206\223\nInspect diff\n\342\206\223\nRun SDK build/typecheck\n\342\206\223\nVerify no public contract regression\n\342\206\223\nProduce report\n\342\206\223\nReady for review\n\nThis must be real dogfooding.\n\nThe application should not secretly bypass the AgentSam SDK when editing the AgentSam SDK.\n\n11. Bootstrap problem\n\nHandle self-hosting carefully.\n\nThe currently running SDK version is:\n\nSDK N\n\nIt creates and tests:\n\nSDK N+1 candidate\n\nSDK N+1 does not replace SDK N during the mission.\n\nInstead:\n\nrunning SDK N\n      \342\224\202\n      \342\226\274\ncandidate workspace\n      \342\224\202\n      \342\226\274\nSDK N+1\n      \342\224\202\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 typecheck\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 unit tests\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 integration tests\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 mission tests\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 benchmark\n      \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 verification\n              \342\224\202\n              \342\226\274\n         review / merge\n\nOnly a subsequent clean run should load the newly accepted SDK.\n\nNever hot-swap an unverified SDK underneath an active mission.\n\n12. Evolution manifest\n\nEvery self-improvement mission should produce an artifact describing:\n\nobjective\nhypothesis\nfiles changed\npublic contracts affected\ntests added\ntests passed\nbenchmarks before\nbenchmarks after\nmodel/token usage\ntool calls\nexecution duration\nregressions\nunresolved concerns\n\nCall this something clean such as:\n\nEvolution Report\n\nDo not create a giant new subsystem just for the name.\n\n13. Regression gates\n\nAgentSam may propose changes to itself freely inside its isolated branch/workspace, but promotion requires gates.\n\nAt minimum:\n\ntypecheck\nSDK unit tests\nintegration tests\npublic API contract tests\nbuild\nlint where configured\nGit diff review\nno accidental secrets\nno unauthorized destructive action\n\nAlso add a small set of self-hosting missions as regression tests.\n\nExample:\n\ninspect this fixture repository\nfind all imports of X\nedit a file\nrun tests\ngenerate diff\nproduce artifact\n\nIf a candidate SDK cannot perform the core AgentSam workflow, it cannot promote.\n\n14. Branch-based autonomy\n\nAgentSam should never autonomously modify the protected production branch.\n\nSelf-evolution should normally operate as:\n\nmain\n \342\224\202\n \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 agentsam/evolve-<mission>\n           \342\224\202\n           \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 inspect\n           \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 edit\n           \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 test\n           \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 benchmark\n           \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 verify\n                   \342\224\202\n                   \342\226\274\n               review / PR\n\nAllow the user to choose whether the final step is:\n\nleave changes\ncommit\nopen PR\n\nDo not silently merge its own changes.\n\n15. SDK telemetry\n\nBecause AgentSam will improve itself, record enough data to know whether a change actually helped.\n\nTrack:\n\nmission success/failure\nmodel\ntokens\nestimated cost\ntool calls\nretries\nfilesystem reads\nsearches\nedits\ncommands\ntests\nelapsed time\nhuman intervention count\n\nAvoid logging hidden reasoning or secrets.\n\nThe important metric is:\n\nsuccessful mission cost and completion quality, not merely number of tool calls.\n\n16. Monaco integration\n\nThe Monaco workspace being built now should consume the SDK filesystem APIs.\n\nIt should let me inspect what AgentSam is changing while a self-hosting mission runs.\n\nI want:\n\nAgent activity     SDK source\n     \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n     \342\224\202                 \342\226\274\n     \342\224\202              Monaco\n     \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n     \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 live diff\n\nDo not create an unrelated second editor.\n\n17. Preview / Code / Changes\n\nPreserve the small product model:\n\nPreview\nCode\nChanges\nArtifacts\n\nFor an SDK mission:\n\nCode = source being modified\n\nChanges = Git diff\n\nArtifacts = Evolution Report, architecture SVG, benchmark results\n\nPreview = app/browser verification when the SDK change affects visible behavior\n\n18. SDK documentation\n\nGenerate useful developer documentation:\n\nGetting Started\nAgentSam Client\nMissions\nEnvironments\nRepository API\nFilesystem API\nTerminal API\nGit API\nBrowser API\nTool Registry\nEvents\nSelf-Hosting\nSafety Model\n\nDocumentation must be generated from actual implemented contracts rather than aspirational APIs that do not exist.\n\n19. CLI\n\nAdd a minimal SDK CLI if the architecture supports it cleanly.\n\nTarget experience:\n\nagentsam inspect .\n\nagentsam mission \\\n  --repo . \\\n  \"find and repair the failing tests\"\n\nagentsam evolve \\\n  \"improve repository search performance\"\n\nThe CLI should call the same SDK as the application.\n\nDo not implement a parallel orchestration engine for the CLI.\n\n20. First self-hosting mission\n\nAfter the SDK vertical slice works, use AgentSam itself to perform one real improvement to the AgentSam SDK.\n\nChoose a small but meaningful task discovered through inspection.\n\nDo not fake the self-hosting demonstration.\n\nI want to watch:\n\nAgentSam SDK\n      \342\206\223\nopens AgentSam SDK\n      \342\206\223\ndiagnoses a real limitation\n      \342\206\223\nchanges AgentSam SDK\n      \342\206\223\ntests AgentSam SDK\n      \342\206\223\ncompares results\n      \342\206\223\npresents the change\n\nShow the complete execution ledger.\n\nProduct principle\n\nAgentSam should become the best tool for developing AgentSam.\n\nEvery infrastructure capability exposed to applications should eventually be usable by AgentSam itself.\n\nHowever:\n\nself-evolution is software development, not uncontrolled mutation.\n\nCandidate changes happen in isolated workspaces, are measurable, tested, reversible, reviewable, and versioned.\n\nCritical implementation constraint\n\nDo not build a demo SDK that simply wraps fake state.\n\nMove existing functional behavior behind real SDK contracts and make the current application consume those contracts.\n\nPrefer:\n\none implementation\n     \342\206\221\nAgentSam SDK\n  \342\206\221       \342\206\221\nApp      CLI\n\nrather than:\n\nfrontend implementation\nCLI implementation\nSDK implementation\nself-evolution implementation\n\nThere must be one authority for each capability.\n\nVerification before stopping\n\nDo not stop at scaffolding.\n\nDemonstrate:\n\nSDK imports successfully.\nApp uses SDK.\nMonaco reads files through SDK.\nSDK can inspect a repository.\nSDK can execute a mission.\nSDK can edit a file in an isolated workspace.\nSDK can run terminal commands/tests.\nSDK can produce a Git diff.\nSDK emits typed execution events.\nUI streams those events.\nAgentSam can target its own SDK.\nA candidate self-change passes/fails gates correctly.\nEvolution Report is generated.\nProduction build passes.\n\nThen run the first genuine AgentSam develops AgentSam mission and show me the result.\n\nThe recursion is the fun part:\n\n                    YOU\n                     \342\224\202\n                     \342\226\274\n               AgentSam App\n                     \342\224\202\n                     \342\226\274\n               AgentSam SDK N\n                     \342\224\202\n                     \342\226\274\n          \"improve AgentSam SDK\"\n                     \342\224\202\n                     \342\226\274\n              candidate N+1\n             \342\225\261      \342\224\202       \342\225\262\n          tests   benchmark   verify\n             \342\225\262      \342\224\202       \342\225\261\n                     \342\226\274\n                  review\n                     \342\224\202\n                     \342\226\274\n                AgentSam N+1\n\nThat turns the SDK from \342\200\234some utilities AgentSam happens to have\342\200\235 into the kernel of the product.\n\nAnd once it works, you get a pretty wild feedback loop: you notice AgentSam sucks at something \342\206\222 tell AgentSam to improve that part of its SDK \342\206\222 it inspects its own telemetry/code \342\206\222 builds a candidate \342\206\222 benchmarks it \342\206\222 you approve the better version \342\206\222 next mission runs on the improved SDK.\n\nThat is the version of \342\200\234self-evolving\342\200\235 I\342\200\231d actually trust. The direction I\342\200\231d give that agent is: stop treating this as a benchmark/demo shell and turn it into the actual authenticated Agent Sam operator workbench you can use to refactor and build InnerAnimalMedia.\n\nPaste this to the agent as the next master instruction:\n\nMission: turn AgentSamRemix into the real Agent Sam Workbench\n\nThe current interface is no longer a preview/demo. Build it as a standalone production application whose purpose is to let Agent Sam inspect, edit, test, verify, and refactor real repositories \342\200\224 beginning with SamPrimeaux/inneranimalmedia.\n\nThe finished application should feel like an actual developer application when opened directly, not an app embedded inside an AI Studio preview.\n\nPreserve the strongest pieces already built:\n\nEngineering Mission\nModel Ladder / model routing\nexecution environment selection\nExecution Ledger\nMonaco Code Workspace\nBrowser Verifier\nCode Mode / tool composition\nNetwork Allowlist\nArchitecture Report\nBackend Comparison\ntelemetry/cost visibility\n\nBut reorganize them into a coherent Agent Sam Workbench rather than a benchmarking dashboard.\n\n1. Agent Sam SDK is the canonical application contract\n\nDo not invent a second authentication system, user table, session format, OAuth implementation, or Agent Sam tool contract in this app.\n\nThe canonical portable dependency is:\n\n@inneranimalmedia/agentsam-sdk\n\nCurrent development package identity is:\n\n@inneranimalmedia/agentsam-sdk\n2.0.0-alpha.identity.11\n\nIntegrate through its public exports/subpath exports. Do not copy SDK source into this app.\n\nDevelopment may use a local linked checkout of agentsam-sdk; deployment should consume a pinned package version.\n\nThe ownership rule is:\n\nagentsam-sdk\n    \342\224\202\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 identity contracts\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 repository intelligence\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 portable runtime contracts\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 reusable Agent Sam capabilities\n            \342\224\202\n            \342\226\274\nAgent Sam Workbench\n            \342\224\202\n            \342\226\274\nInnerAnimalMedia host adapters / MCP / infrastructure\n\nHost-specific credentials and bindings stay in this application/server environment. Portable logic stays in the SDK.\n\n2. Use the real Agent Sam Identity package\n\nThe SDK already contains:\n\nimport {\n  createIdentityClient,\n  createIdentityService,\n  createCloudflareD1Adapter,\n  handleIdentityWorkerRequest,\n} from \'@inneranimalmedia/agentsam-sdk/identity\';\n\nDo not create fake auth screens backed by localStorage.\n\nUse the SDK Worker identity implementation.\n\nExisting canonical routes are:\n\nPOST /api/auth/login\nPOST /api/auth/signup\nPOST /api/auth/logout\nGET  /api/auth/me\n\nPOST /api/auth/password-reset/request\nPOST /api/auth/password-reset/confirm\n\nGET /api/oauth/iam/start\nGET /api/oauth/iam/callback\n\nGET /api/oauth/google/start\nGET /api/oauth/google/callback\n\nGET /api/oauth/github/start\nGET /api/oauth/github/callback\n\nGET   /api/company\nPATCH /api/company\n\n/auth/login\n/auth/signup\n/auth/reset\n\nThe default OAuth lane is InnerAnimalMedia IAM, using minted:\n\nIAM_CLIENT_ID\nIAM_CLIENT_SECRET\n\nDeveloper Google/GitHub BYOK remains supported when their credential pairs exist.\n\nNever expose client secrets, Cloudflare tokens, MCP credentials, database credentials, or provider secrets to React/Vite/browser code.\n\n3. Make auth a real application boundary\n\nStructure the app so:\n\n/\n  \342\206\223\nauthenticated?\n  \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 no  \342\206\222 /auth/login\n  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 yes \342\206\222 /dashboard/workbench\n\nUse the SDK\'s authenticated /dashboard/* behavior instead of creating another auth guard implementation unless a tiny host adapter is necessary.\n\nThe actual application should live under:\n\n/dashboard/workbench\n\nwith optional child routes:\n\n/dashboard/workbench\n/dashboard/workbench/repositories\n/dashboard/workbench/browser\n/dashboard/workbench/terminal\n/dashboard/workbench/runs\n/dashboard/workbench/architecture\n/dashboard/workbench/settings\n\nA page refresh on any route must preserve authentication and restore the application normally.\n\nGET /api/auth/me is the browser\'s authoritative current-user check.\n\nDo not consider a client-side boolean such as isLoggedIn=true authentication.\n\n4. Cloudflare-native application boundary\n\nBuild this as a real Cloudflare application.\n\nServer/Worker owns:\n\nauthentication\nauthorization\nsecrets\nD1\nKV\nR2\nDurable Objects\nMCP calls\nGitHub calls\nterminal execution\nAgent Sam tool execution\napproval enforcement\ntelemetry writes\nprovider calls\n\nBrowser owns:\n\napplication shell\nMonaco\nmission composition\nvisual tool state\nexecution stream\ndiff presentation\nbrowser preview\napprovals UI\ntelemetry visualization\n\nBrowser code must never directly possess infrastructure credentials.\n\nStart with the bindings already expected by Agent Sam Identity:\n\nDB\nASSETS\nSESSION_CACHE\n\nand support the existing password-reset email integration through:\n\nRESEND_API_KEY\n\nDo not invent binding names for other services merely for visual completeness. Add a binding only when there is an implementation consuming it.\n\n5. This application is an engineering workbench, not another IDE clone\n\nThe central primitive is a Mission.\n\nA mission might be:\n\n\"Finish the InnerAnimalMedia src/ retirement\"\n\n\"Audit authentication overlap and eliminate duplicate authorities\"\n\n\"Repair the mobile chat composer and verify it in Browser Run\"\n\n\"Inspect agentsam-sdk and extract reusable repository tooling\"\n\nA mission becomes:\n\nMission\n  \342\206\223\nrepository context\n  \342\206\223\nAgent Sam plan\n  \342\206\223\ntool execution loop\n  \342\206\223\ncode/files changed\n  \342\206\223\ntests\n  \342\206\223\nbrowser verification\n  \342\206\223\narchitecture / dependency verification\n  \342\206\223\nreviewable diff\n  \342\206\223\ncommit / PR / deploy if approved\n\nThis flow should become the backbone of the UI.\n\nMonaco is a window into the mission, not the product itself.\n\n6. Repository connection\n\nBuild a proper Repository Workspace model.\n\nInitially support:\n\nSamPrimeaux/inneranimalmedia\nSamPrimeaux/agentsam-sdk\n\nbut do not hardcode Agent Sam\'s architecture around those names.\n\nA repository workspace should expose:\n\nrepository\nbranch/ref\nworking tree status\ncurrent mission\nchanged files\nactive files\nrepo intelligence snapshot\nexecution environment\nterminal connection\nbrowser target\nactive run\napprovals\n\nRepository intelligence should come from the SDK\'s new portable:\n\nagentsam_sdk.repository.intelligence\n\nIt already discovers arbitrary repository layouts rather than assuming src/, backend/, etc.\n\nPresent useful evidence such as:\n\nactive file tree\nlanguage mix\nmanifests\ndirectory density\ncurrent churn\nhot files\npressure points\nstability\n\nLater this should accept dependency/entrypoint graph data without redesigning the UI.\n\n7. Execution environments\n\nDo not make Cloudflare vs Google Antigravity the identity of the app.\n\nThose are execution backends.\n\nModel them generically:\n\nExecution Environment\n\nLocal\nRemote\nSandbox\nCloudflare\nGoogle / Antigravity\n\nEvery environment should report a common capability packet:\n\ninterface ExecutionEnvironment {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  status: \'offline\' | \'starting\' | \'ready\' | \'busy\' | \'error\';\n  capabilities: {\n    filesystem: boolean;\n    terminal: boolean;\n    browser: boolean;\n    network: boolean;\n    git: boolean;\n    isolated: boolean;\n  };\n}\n\nThe UI then chooses the appropriate environment without hardwiring mission logic to one provider.\n\nPreserve the nice environment lifecycle concept:\n\nSpinning up environment\342\200\246\nPreparing workspace\342\200\246\nReady\n8. Execution stream should use progressive disclosure\n\nThe default mission view should remain calm.\n\nRepresent activity chronologically:\n\nThought\nInspect repository\n\nRun Command\nnpm test\n\nRead File\nbackend/agentsam/...\n\nEdit File\n...\n\nBrowser Verify\n...\n\nEach execution row is expandable.\n\nCollapsed state:\n\n\342\234\223 Run Command     npm test                 4.8s\n\nExpanded:\n\ncommand\ncwd\nenvironment\nstdout\nstderr\nexit code\nduration\nrelated files\nreceipt/tool-call ID\n\nDo not permanently dump terminal logs into the main experience.\n\n9. Respect Agent Sam safety/execution semantics\n\nRead operations should be the default.\n\nClearly distinguish:\n\nREAD\nWRITE\nEXECUTE\nEXTERNAL EFFECT\nDESTRUCTIVE\n\nAnything requiring approval must visibly pause the mission and ask for approval.\n\nNever fake an approval by continuing locally.\n\nExamples requiring explicit handling:\n\ngit push\nmerge\ndeploy\ndatabase mutation\nsecret change\nproduction write\ndestructive filesystem operation\nexternal message/send\n\nPreserve an execution receipt/audit trail for every meaningful tool operation.\n\n10. Network allowlist\n\nKeep the Network & Allowlist surface, but make it operational rather than decorative.\n\nIt should show:\n\ndomain\nreason\nenvironment\nrequested by\nallowed/blocked\ntemporary/persistent\n\nUse progressive disclosure.\n\nA normal user shouldn\'t have to stare at network policy while coding.\n\n11. Replace benchmark language\n\nRemove copy that makes this look primarily like:\n\n\"telemetry benchmarker\"\n\"Cloudflare vs Google comparison experiment\"\n\nBackend comparison can remain an advanced diagnostics panel.\n\nMain product language should be:\n\nAgent Sam\nEngineering Workbench\nAutonomous software execution\nRepository workspace\nMission\nRun\nVerify\nReview\n\nThe workbench is allowed to benchmark environments internally, but benchmarking is not the product.\n\n12. Real standalone app shell\n\nRemove any visual feeling of:\n\ndemo in a card\ncentered preview canvas\nfake desktop contained inside another desktop\nexcessive permanent borders around the entire application\n\nThe application should occupy the viewport.\n\nDesktop shell:\n\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202 workspace/repo       Agent Sam          run/status \342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\244\n\342\224\202           \342\224\202                                         \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 nav       \342\224\202 current mission/workspace               \342\224\202\n\342\224\202           \342\224\202                                         \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n\nUse the current visual personality \342\200\224 dark engineering surfaces, subtle glass, restrained status colors \342\200\224 but simplify it.\n\nAvoid filling every inch with pills and badges.\n\nImportant state should be visible; implementation trivia should be expandable.\n\n13. Make InnerAnimalMedia the first real proof\n\nThe first production acceptance case is:\n\nauthenticate as an IAM user\n    \342\206\223\nopen SamPrimeaux/inneranimalmedia\n    \342\206\223\ninspect repository\n    \342\206\223\nbegin an engineering mission\n    \342\206\223\nAgent Sam reads relevant files\n    \342\206\223\nexecutes tools over the appropriate environment\n    \342\206\223\nedits repository\n    \342\206\223\nruns tests\n    \342\206\223\nverifies browser behavior\n    \342\206\223\nshows architecture/dependency impact\n    \342\206\223\nproduces reviewable diff\n    \342\206\223\nasks before commit/push/deploy\n\nIf that works, this is an application.\n\nIf we can only click tabs containing simulated data, it is still a prototype.\n\n14. Do not rebuild existing InnerAnimalMedia backend logic inside this app\n\nInnerAnimalMedia already owns the host infrastructure and Agent Sam runtime.\n\nConnect to it through explicit API/MCP/service adapters.\n\nDo not fork:\n\nauthentication authority\ntool catalog authority\ntelemetry authority\nbrowser authority\nterminal authority\nmodel routing authority\nrepository contracts\n\nThis workbench is a client/operator surface plus its thin host Worker.\n\nWe are actively refactoring InnerAnimalMedia to eliminate duplicated authorities. Do not introduce new ones here.\n\n15. Implementation sequence\n\nWork in this order:\n\nConvert preview layout into full standalone application shell.\nInstall/wire Agent Sam SDK.\nWire real SDK Identity Worker routes.\nAdd login/session/logout and authenticated application routing.\nEstablish Repository Workspace contract.\nTurn current Engineering Mission into the primary mission object.\nNormalize execution backend abstraction.\nConnect execution ledger to real tool/run events.\nConnect Monaco to real repository files/diffs.\nConnect Browser Verifier to actual mission verification.\nConnect repository intelligence.\nWire approvals.\nPersist/recover current mission/workspace.\nRemove all mock data that can now be backed by reality.\nAdd production build/deployment config.\n\nDo not rebuild the entire UI before wiring the contracts.\n\nDefinition of done\n\nI should be able to open the deployed application in a normal browser window and:\n\nbe redirected to Agent Sam auth when signed out;\nsign in through real IAM OAuth;\nrestore my session after refresh;\nsee my authenticated identity;\nselect/connect a repository;\nrun repository intelligence;\ncreate a mission;\nwatch real Agent Sam tool execution;\ninspect individual tool receipts;\nopen/edit actual repository files;\nsee an actual diff;\nexecute tests in a selected environment;\nverify the result in the browser;\nstop for approval on meaningful writes;\nrecover the mission after reload;\nand ultimately operate on SamPrimeaux/inneranimalmedia without adding another duplicate backend authority.\n\nDo not optimize for screenshot completeness. Optimize for one completely real vertical slice.\n\nStart by auditing the current generated project against this specification. Preserve working components. Identify mocks and duplicate authorities. Then implement the smallest complete authenticated vertical slice before expanding any secondary feature.\n\nThat gives the AI Studio agent a much better target than \342\200\234make this an actual app.\342\200\235 The key architectural shift is:\n\nCURRENT\nAgentSamRemix\n  = impressive simulated/benchmark workbench\n\nTARGET\nAgent Sam Workbench\n  = authenticated operator client\n       \342\206\223\n    AgentSam SDK\n       \342\206\223\nInnerAnimalMedia / MCP / execution infrastructure\n       \342\206\223\nreal repository\n\nAnd I especially would not have it build a new auth implementation. I checked current agentsam-sdk/main: the SDK Worker router already has real email login/signup/logout/session, password reset, IAM OAuth, Google/GitHub OAuth, company branding, D1-backed identity, and authenticated /dashboard/* routing. The app should consume that authority and fill any missing SDK seam rather than creating AgentSamRemixAuthService.ts or some other future cleanup project."
    }
  }
}
